{
  "raw": {
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/FAU-Medicine---Galen-Building/Lead-Clinical-Medical-Assistant_REQ22894": {
      "title": "Lead Clinical Medical Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Florida Atlantic University Medical Group is seeking a Lead Clinical Medical Assistant in Boca Raton, FL. The Lead Clinical Medical Assistant supports the Clinical Supervisor in overseeing daily   clinical operations and serves as a key resource and leader for the Medical Assistant team. This position serves as a role model in demonstrating sound judgement, maintaining professionalism, and supporting the Clinical Supervisor in maintaining a safe, efficient, and patient centered environment. This position helps ensure patient flow, consistent clinical standards, accurate   documentation, and compliance with organizational policies and procedures. P rovides day-to-day guidance, training, and support to clinical   sta ff while maintaining a strong focus on patient care and service excellence.   Key Responsibilities:   Serve as a clinical resource and point of contact for Medical Assistants and clinical   support sta ff .   Assists the Clinical Supervisor with daily coordination of clinical operations and   workflow.   Monitor patient flow and help identify and resolve operational or clinical workflow   issues.   Provide guidance, coaching, and support to Medical Assistants to promote   consistent performance and adherence to established standards.   Assist with onboarding, orientation, training, and competency assessment of new   clinical sta ff .   Support implementation and maintenance of clinical policies, procedures, and best   practices.   Help ensure exam rooms, equipment, supplies, and clinical areas are properly   maintained and prepared for patient care.   Monitor compliance with infection prevention, safety, documentation, and   regulatory requirements.   Assist with sta ff scheduling, coverage, and workflow assignments as directed by the   Clinical Supervisor.   Perform and oversee appropriate clinical duties within the scope of practice of the   Medical Assistant role.   Promote accurate and timely documentation in the electronic medical record.   Assist providers and clinical sta ff with patient care, procedures, and coordination of   services.   Identify performance, workflow, or patient-care concerns and communicate them   promptly to the Clinical Supervisor.   Participate in quality improvement initiatives, audits, and clinical process   improvement projects.   Promote a positive, professional, and collaborative work environment.   Provide exceptional patient service and model appropriate communication and   professionalism.   Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Clinical Supervisor or   leadership.   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB     Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of appropriate experience required. Current Medical Assistant certification/registration required. Current BLS/CPR certification required or obtainable within the required timeframe. Excellent communication, organizational, problem-solving, and interpersonal skills required. Ability to prioritize multiple responsibilities and work effectively in a fast-paced clinical environment required. Strong knowledge of clinical workflows, patient care procedures, infection control, and medical documentation required. Completion of an accredited Medical Assistant program preferred. Minimum of 2–3 years of clinical Medical Assistant experience preferred. Previous leadership, mentoring, or lead experience preferred. Salary: $25.00 Hourly. College or Department: OPS - COM: Clinical Services Personnel Location: FAU Medicine - Galen Building Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:30 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-19 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Title-II-Digital-Accessibility-Manual-Testing-Coordinator--Student-Accessibility-Services_REQ22975": {
      "title": "Title II Digital Accessibility Manual Testing Coordinator, Student Accessibility Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Title II Digital Accessibility Manual Testing Coordinator. - Boca Raton, FL. Summary of responsibilities: Conducts comprehensive manual accessibility testing of websites, web applications, software, mobile applications, and digital documents using established accessibility standards, including WCAG 2.1 Level AA and Section 508. Performs manual testing using keyboard-only navigation, screen readers, assistive technologies, browser accessibility features, and other appropriate testing methods to identify accessibility barriers that may not be detected through automated testing. Evaluates digital documents, including PDFs and other electronic content, for accessibility, structure, navigation, reading order, headings, alternative text, tables, forms, links, and other applicable accessibility requirements. Documents accessibility findings in clear, actionable reports that identify the location of each issue, applicable WCAG success criterion or accessibility requirement, description of the barrier, impact, and recommended technical remediation. Tracks accessibility issues through resolution and maintains documentation of testing results, remediation activities, and outstanding barriers. Collaborates with OIT, Public Service, OCR9, SAS, the College for Online Learning and Continuing Education, and other university stakeholders to support consistent implementation of digital accessibility requirements. Provides training and technical assistance on Section 508, WCAG 2.1 Level AA, manual accessibility testing, accessible document creation, and faculty and staff responsibilities for developing accessible digital content. Serves on the Title II Accessibility Committee and contributes to the development, review, and implementation of accessibility policies, procedures, and practices. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.   State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.   State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.   Sick Leave Pool Program.   Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).   Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).     For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $51,000. annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Some weekends and nights are required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Associate-General-Counsel_REQ23012": {
      "title": "Associate General Counsel",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Associate General Counsel. - Boca Raton, FL. Responsible to the General Counsel. Provides primary in-house counsel on a broad array of external transactional arrangements, including contract and lease negotiation, drafting, and compliance. May be delegated responsibility for the overall direction and management of specific areas of the legal function of the Board of Trustees or the university. Assists as directed by the General Counsel in planning, organizing, and directing all legal activities involving the Board of Trustees or the university. Advises and consults with university or Board officials on legal rights and obligations and assists in the formulation of legal policy. Summary of Responsibilities: Responsible for managing university litigation and administrative law matters, including coordinating with the State’s Division of Risk Management on the selection and assignment of outside counsel, overseeing discovery, trial preparation, mediation, and settlement negotiations.   Provides legal advice to the Division of Student Affairs on a variety of issues related to student discipline, crisis response, academics, financial matters, residency, contracts, international programs, Title IX, the Americans with Disabilities Act, free speech, and religious accommodations.  Supervises the University’s processes for subpoena responses and document production and advises institutional clients on compliance with Florida’s public records laws and Federal privacy laws.  Serves as a liaison to the University Police Department, the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX, Public Affairs, and the University’s Risk Manager. Appears and attends at court and mediation as necessary. Performs other job-related duties as required or deemed appropriate. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:   Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.   State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.   State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.   Sick Leave Pool Program.   Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).   Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).     For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Juris doctor degree from an accredited institution and two years of appropriate experience is required. Salary: $165,000.00 - $185,000.00 USD Annually. Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP) College or Department: Office of University General Counsel Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00am - 5:00pm Application Deadline: 2026-10-26 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Contract-Administrator_REQ22176": {
      "title": "Contract Administrator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Contract Administrator in Boca Raton, FL. The Contract Administrator plays a critical role in supporting the Office of Sponsored Programs (OSP). Responsible for drafting, reviewing, negotiating, and administering a wide range of sponsored research agreements. Ensures compliance with federal, state, sponsor, and institutional requirements, while fostering effective communication and strong working relationships with faculty, staff, sponsors, and collaborators. Summary of Responsibilities: Review, draft, redline, and negotiate externally funded research agreements, amendments, and non-financial agreements such as NDAs and MOUs from federal, state, foundation, and local government agencies. Works with FAU General Counsel and coordinates with other internal offices such as Export Control, IT, Research Integrity, Technology Development to address intellectual property, indemnification, publication rights, data use, confidentiality, and regulatory compliance (Institutional Review Board (IRB), Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC), Institutional Biosafety Committee (IBC), etc.). Obtain required legal approvals for contractual documents and facilitate their execution in accordance with delegated signature authority. Serve as backup for the issuance of outgoing subaward and the complete subaward process. Serve as a resource to OSP staff and stakeholders on complex contracting issues and interpretation of contractual terms. Contribute to the continuous improvement of internal contract and subaward processes in alignment with university policies and compliance standards. Maintain accurate records, logs, documentation, and electronic files related to contracts and outgoing subawards. Stay current on evolving federal and state regulations, sponsor requirements, and institutional policies. Attend relevant regional meetings, trainings, and professional development activities as appropriate. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Strong organizational and communication skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously required. Strong written and verbal communication skills required. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills required. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and external partners required. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines required. Knowledge of federal, state, and sponsor regulations, including Uniform Guidance required. Demonstrates experience in contract management, contract drafting, negotiation, and compliance required. Preferred experience in contract negotiation, research administration, or grants management. Salary: $65,000 - $72,000 annually. College or Department: Division of Research: Sponsored Programs Contract Administration Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-26 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. This is a research or research-related support position. As required by Florida Statutes Section 1010.35, a Foreign Influence Screening may be required. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Laboratory-Assistant_REQ22973": {
      "title": "Laboratory Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Department of Psychology at Florida Atlantic University is seeking a highly motivated part-time Laboratory Assistant in Boca Raton, FL. The research for Dr. Pehlivanoglu's lab investigates resilience and vulnerability in cognitive, affective, and social functioning across adulthood and aging by employing a multimethod approach that integrates behavioral experiments/surveys with physiological (e.g., eye-tracking) and neuroimaging (EEG/ERP, and fMRI) measures. The Laboratory Assistant will play a central role in establishing a new laboratory from the ground up while receiving extensive mentorship in research design, cognitive neuroscience methods, EEG and fMRI data acquisition and analysis, statistical analysis, and scientific writing. The position also offers extensive training in cognitive and affective aging research within a collaborative and supportive research environment. The Laboratory Assistant will also have opportunities to contribute to scientific publications and conference presentations. This is a part-time, 1-year position with the possibility of renewal for a second year based on performance. This position is ideal for an individual interested in pursuing training in neuroscience, psychology, biomedical engineering, computer science, cognitive science, or a related field after gaining intensive research experience. The Laboratory Assistant will work closely with the principal investigator on all aspects of research, including: Assisting with the establishment of laboratory infrastructure and research workflows. Setting up, maintaining, and troubleshooting EEG or other research equipment. Developing and optimizing EEG preprocessing and analysis pipelines. Assisting with fMRI preprocessing and analysis pipelines. Programming behavioral experiments (e.g., PsychoPy, PsychoJS, E-Prime, MATLAB). Participating in study design, project development, and interpretation of research findings. Managing research databases and ensuring high-quality data organization. Assisting with participant recruitment, scheduling, and testing. Supervising and training undergraduate research assistants. Assisting with statistical analyses, data visualization, and reproducible research workflows. Contributing to manuscript preparation, conference presentations, and grant-related activities. Performing general laboratory management and administrative tasks as needed. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Explore Living in Palm Beach County   Florida Atlantic University has six different campuses. The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma or equivalent from an accredited institution is required. Salary: $18.00 USD - $23.00 USD hourly Non-Exempt Other Personnel Service (OPS) College or Department: College of Science Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, part-time up to 29 hours. Application Deadline: 2026-10-23 Special Instructions to Applicant: Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Chair-and-Professor_REQ22774-1": {
      "title": "Chair and Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Chair and Professor- Boca Raton, FL The College of Education (COE) at Florida Atlantic University is accepting applications for department chair of Curriculum and Instruction ( https://www.fau.edu/education/academicdepartments/curriculum-instruction/ ). The department chair serves as senior faculty member and administrator of the academic department. At the departmental level, this person is responsible for faculty recruitment and development; instructional program development and quality enhancement; coordination of departmental research and service programs; evaluation of personnel; and, through the dean, representing the department within and beyond the university. The chair also maintains relationships with students, other administrators, university councils and committees, alumni, professional organizations, and various other public and private groups. In conjunction with the COE dean, the chair develops the department's annual budget request, manages the course schedule of the department’s 15+ undergraduate and graduate programs, administers expenditures of the allocated funds, works closely with department program coordinators and program committees, evaluates faculty and staff, and manages other resources available to the department. The chair facilitates effective relationships within and across department programs and, as a member of the COE's leadership team, works collaboratively with the dean and other unit leaders to guide the work of the COE. The COE at Florida Atlantic University is committed to providing an accessible and supportive environment that promotes academic excellence and prepares all students for success in a broad range of educational and professional contexts. Candidates who can contribute to that goal are encouraged to apply and to identify their strengths in this area. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral Degree in Curriculum and Instruction or related area from an accredited institution; hold rank of full professor at the time of appointment required. Preferred Qualifications: • Leadership in preservice and in-service teacher education or related areas. • Administrative, managerial, and financial knowledge and skills to effectively lead an academic department. • Success as a collaborative leader, with effective communication and interpersonal skills in an environment that encourages engagement with varied perspectives and experiences. • Record of teaching/ research/ service demonstrating commitment to public education. • Experience and success working in constructive partnerships with large school districts. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Department of Curriculum and Instruction Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-11-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three professional letters of recommendation. In the event that individuals writing letters of recommendation wish to remain confidential, please email letters to the search committee chair, Dr. Elizabeth Sacks (evillare@fau.edu). Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/OPS-Physician_REQ22903": {
      "title": "OPS Physician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking multiple Physicians in the Department of Student Health Services. - Boca Raton, FL. Student Health Services at Florida Atlantic University invites applicants for a temporary part-time Physician. Florida Atlantic University (FAU) Student Health Services is located in beautiful Boca Raton with additional smaller campuses in Jupiter and Davie. FAU is an exciting and dynamic school that is rapidly growing. At FAU SHS, we seek to provide high quality, culturally competent care in a manner that is respectful, fiscally responsible, and developmentally appropriate. We combine a wide range of medical, counseling, preventative, and wellness services to help students remain healthy and succeed academically.  Summary of Responsibilities Include:  Obtains appropriate medical history and performs accurate physical examination.  Comforts with acute medical care, primary care, and chronic disease management.  Experience with basic primary care procedures such as laceration repairs and pap smears.  Orders and correctly interprets appropriate diagnostic studies to assist with management.  Develops an appropriate assessment and treatment plan consistent with findings and utilizes medication and other treatment modalities appropriately.  Provides education and information on the diagnosis and treatment plan including appropriate preventive and health enhancement strategies and actions.  Refers for additional consultation, evaluation, and treatment when clinically indicated.  Practices within the scope of privileges and licensure.  Uses evidence-based strategies to guide diagnosis and treatment.  Adheres to policies and established workflows for delivery of patient care.  Boca Raton – Main Campus OPS physicians will serve as the Provider of the Day and will: Serve as the primary clinical resource for nurses, NPs, and PAs, providing guidance and support for clinical questions. Provide clinical support and coverage for day-to-day OPS operations. Jupiter – Satellite Campus OPS physicians will provide support for: OPS provider inbox coverage, including addressing clinical questions and follow-up needs. Inventory support, including assisting with inventory-related needs and coordination. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).    For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County  The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Doctor of Medicine (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine (DO) degree from an accredited institution or college of osteopathic medicine required. Unrestricted MD or DO License to practice in state of Florida by date of hire. Board certification in internal medicine, medicine-pediatrics, or family practice. DEA registration. Current BLS certification. Experience using electronic health records. Demonstrated ability to provide culturally competent care for diverse population. Strong interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills. Highly effective problem solving and decisions making skills. The provider must be willing to travel between the Main Campus in Boca Raton and the satellite campus in Jupiter, as needed. Salary: $115 hourly. Other Personnel Services (OPS) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs: Student Health Services Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am - 5pm. Application Deadline: 2026-10-22 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
