    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/American-Sign-Language-Interpreter_REQ22831": {
      "title": "American Sign Language Interpreter",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-29\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an American Sign Language Interpreter in Boca Raton, FL. The OPS Part-Time ASL Interpreter provides American Sign Language (ASL) interpretation services to support a deaf faculty member within the College of Medicine. The interpreter will facilitate effective communication during meetings, presentations, conferences, research activities, trainings, and other university-related events. Summary of Responsibilities: Provide accurate and professional ASL interpretation services for faculty meetings, presentations, seminars, and departmental events. Interpret communications involving medical education, healthcare, scientific research, and academic discussions. Facilitate communication between the faculty member and colleagues, students, researchers, healthcare professionals, and external collaborators. Review meeting materials and presentation content in advance when available to ensure familiarity with technical terminology and subject matter. Maintain strict confidentiality regarding research activities, patient-related information, and university business in accordance with applicable privacy and confidentiality requirements. Collaborate with faculty and departmental staff to coordinate interpretation needs and scheduling. Attend in-person and virtual meetings as needed. Adhere to the professional standards and code of ethics established by the Registry of Interpreters for the Deaf (RID). Other job-related duties as assigned. Explore Living in Palm Beach County   Florida Atlantic University has six different campuses. The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma or equivalent is required. Fluency in American Sign Language (ASL) and English required. RID Certification (NIC or CI/CT), or equivalent professional credentials required. Experience providing ASL interpretation services in higher education, healthcare, medical, scientific, or research settings required. Strong knowledge of professional interpreting practices and ethics required. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills required. Ability to accurately interpret complex medical and scientific terminology required. Ability to work collaboratively with all levels of faculty, staff, and students. Exceptional verbal and written communication skills are essential for success in this position required. Exceptional customer service, organizational and time management skills required. Experience in a higher education institution, medical school, or hospital highly preferred. Salary: $55.00 Hourly. College or Department: OPS - COM: Population Health Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Part time up to 15 hours weekly Monday - Friday. Application Deadline: 2026-10-13 Special Instructions to Applicant: Temporary positions are not established positions and are paid from OPS funds. Temporary positions are usually not eligible for benefits and retirement; however, they may be eligible for health insurance coverage depending on the average hours worked per week. They provide full-time or part-time employment in an exempt or non-exempt employment situation based on job duties and salary in accordance with the Fair Labor Standards Act (FLSA). Temporary positions do not have layoff rights and may be terminated without prior notice. Applicants hired into Temporary positions may apply for a regular appointment should a vacancy become available. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Acute-Care-Surgeon--Emergency-General-Surgery---Surgical-Critical-Care----Assistant-Professor-Associate-Professor-Full-Professor_REQ22950": {
      "title": "Acute Care Surgeon (Emergency General Surgery & Surgical Critical Care) - Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Full Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Department of Surgery at Florida Atlantic University (FAU) seeks a full-time academic surgeon who is board certified/eligible in General Surgery and Surgical Critical Care. The primary responsibility of this position is to serve as a Surgical Critical Care physician, providing comprehensive management of critically ill surgical patients in the intensive care unit. The faculty member will also participate in General Surgery call and have a significant role in the education, supervision, and mentorship of FAU General Surgery residents.   The faculty member will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Surgery and work collaboratively with the General Surgery Residency Program Director and Department leadership.   Responsibilities Serve primarily as a Surgical Critical Care/ICU attending, providing approximately 14–16 daytime ICU shifts per month, generally 12-hour shifts. Direct daily multidisciplinary ICU rounds and management of critically ill postoperative and surgical patients. Manage complex critical care conditions including respiratory failure, mechanical ventilation, sepsis and septic shock, hemodynamic instability, multiorgan failure, acute kidney injury, nutritional and metabolic disorders, and complex postoperative complications. Perform appropriate critical care procedures within clinical privileges, including airway management, central venous and arterial catheter placement, and other bedside procedures. Provide critical care consultation and coordinate care with surgical and multidisciplinary teams. Participate in ICU quality improvement, patient safety, and morbidity and mortality activities. Participate in approximately 4–5 General Surgery call assignments per month, including evaluation and management of acute surgical conditions, inpatient consultation, operative care, and perioperative management. This is not a trauma surgery position; trauma surgery will not be a primary clinical responsibility. Provide direct supervision and bedside teaching of General Surgery residents in the ICU and during General Surgery call. Participate in resident evaluations, curriculum development, didactic conferences, M&M conferences, journal clubs, case conferences, and other educational activities. Maintain an educational environment consistent with ACGME and FAU standards. The successful candidate will receive an academic faculty appointment in the Florida Atlantic University Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine, Department of Surgery, with academic rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. • Completion of an ACGME-accredited General Surgery residency. • Board certification/eligibility in General Surgery. • Fellowship training and board certification/eligibility in Surgical Critical Care. • Eligibility for an unrestricted Florida medical license and appropriate clinical privileges. • Demonstrated commitment to academic medicine, graduate medical education, teaching, and resident mentorship. Salary: Commensurate with qualifications and experience. College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Associate-Program-Director--General-Surgery--Assistant-Professor-Associate-Professor-Full-Professor-_REQ22949": {
      "title": "Associate Program Director, General Surgery (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Florida Atlantic University Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine, Department of Surgery, is seeking a highly qualified, academically accomplished, and motivated Associate Program Director (APD) for the General Surgery Residency Program. The APD will serve as a senior member of the residency leadership team and will work closely with the Chair, Program Director, faculty, residents, and institutional leadership to support the continued development and excellence of the program. The APD will assist in the educational, clinical, administrative, and operational leadership of the residency program, including curriculum development, resident education and evaluation, clinical and operative experience, scheduling and rotation management, recruitment, faculty engagement, scholarly activity, quality improvement, patient safety, resident wellness, and ACGME/ABS compliance.    The APD will participate actively in resident conferences, M&M, Clinical Competency Committee activities, recruitment, mentorship, and continuous program improvement, with a particular emphasis on developing technically proficient, academically engaged, ethical, accountable, and independent surgeons.   The APD will report to the Chair of the Department of Surgery and General Surgery Residency Program Director and will function as a key leadership partner in advancing the mission and strategic goals of the FAU Department of Surgery and General Surgery Residency Program. The APD will provide leadership in resident education, faculty development, clinical operations, resident assessment, recruitment, scholarly activity, quality improvement, and program development while maintaining strong and collaborative relationships with residents, faculty, service chiefs, hospital leadership, affiliated clinical sites, and the FAU Office of Graduate Medical Education. The APD will be expected to identify opportunities for improvement, develop and implement innovative educational initiatives, promote accountability and professionalism, support resident and faculty development, and contribute meaningfully to the continued growth and success of the residency program.   The successful candidate will be an ABS board-certified surgeon with a demonstrated commitment to graduate medical education, surgical education, patient safety, quality improvement, and resident professional development. Prior experience in GME leadership, ACGME accreditation, resident evaluation, recruitment, simulation, or quality improvement is preferred.   The position will include protected administrative time appropriate to the scope and responsibilities of the role and will be evaluated annually based on educational outcomes, resident development, operative experience, recruitment and retention, scholarly activity, faculty engagement, patient safety, quality improvement, accreditation performance, leadership, and contribution to the continued advancement of the program. The successful candidate will receive an academic faculty appointment in the Florida Atlantic University Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine, Department of Surgery, with academic rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. • Completion of an ACGME-accredited General Surgery residency. • Board certification/eligibility in General Surgery. • Eligibility for an unrestricted Florida medical license and appropriate clinical privileges. • Demonstrated commitment to academic medicine, graduate medical education, teaching, and resident mentorship. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Harbor-Branch-HBOI/Executive-Director-of-Harbor-Branch-Oceanographic-Institute_REQ22917": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Executive Director of Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute- Ft Pierce, FL. The Executive Director of the Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute (HBOI) provides visionary leadership to advance the Institute as a world-class center for oceanographic research, innovation, and impact. Reporting to the Vice President for Research, this position drives scientific excellence, industry engagement, strategic partnerships, and resource development while strengthening HBOI's national and international reputation. The Executive Director leads the growth of HBOI's research enterprise, expands external funding opportunities, cultivates relationships with government, industry, philanthropic, and academic partners, and fosters interdisciplinary collaboration across Florida Atlantic University. The role oversees the Institute's research, operational, administrative, and financial functions, including stewardship of HBOI's unique waterfront campus and specialized facilities, while creating opportunities for faculty, staff, and students to contribute to solving critical coastal, ocean, and environmental challenges. As HBOI's chief ambassador, the Executive Director champions innovation, entrepreneurship, workforce development, and transformative research that advances ocean discovery, environmental sustainability, and economic development. Summary of Responsibilities: Provide the vision and leadership necessary to advance HBOI as a world-class oceanographic research and innovation institute. Advance and strengthen HBOI’s core environmental, coast, and ocean research enterprise, supporting scientific excellence and growth in areas such as marine ecosystem conservation, coastal and ocean health, water quality, aquaculture and food security, marine biotechnology, ocean exploration, coastal defenses, and related fields. Serve as the primary external ambassador for HBOI, developing strong relationships with industry executives, government leaders, federal agencies, donors, research organizations, and other strategic partners. Develop and execute a comprehensive strategy for industry engagement and collaboration, including attracting companies to conduct research, testing, and technology development at HBOI. Work with university leadership to establish a consistent framework for industry partnerships that ensures appropriate returns to FAU through sponsored research, student experiences, faculty collaboration, infrastructure investment, and other institutional benefits. Significantly increase sponsored research and diversify HBOI’s funding portfolio, with particular emphasis on federal, defense, industry, and other external research support. Identify and cultivate opportunities for large-scale multidisciplinary and multi-institutional research programs and partnerships. Build interdisciplinary research initiatives that connect environmental and marine science with ocean engineering, autonomous systems, artificial intelligence, biotechnology, and other emerging technologies to address complex coastal and ocean challenges. Expand connections with the defense, maritime, autonomous systems, ocean technology, biotechnology, and related industries where HBOI and FAU have distinctive capabilities. Create meaningful pathways for students to engage with industry through internships, research experiences, sponsored projects, workforce development, and employment opportunities. Work collaboratively with faculty at HBOI and throughout Florida Atlantic to strengthen interdisciplinary research and identify opportunities to connect faculty expertise with industry and government needs. Develop relationships with federal and state agencies and strengthen HBOI’s visibility and competitiveness for major research initiatives and funding opportunities. Work closely with the Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute Foundation and its Board of Directors to align Foundation activities with the strategic needs and opportunities of HBOI and to expand external engagement. Partner with Florida Atlantic’s advancement team to identify and cultivate philanthropic support for HBOI priorities. Lead a diverse and effective team and provide oversight of the Institute’s research, administrative, operational, and budgetary functions. Provide strategic oversight and stewardship of HBOI’s complex 144-acre waterfront campus and 32 facilities, including specialized laboratories, engineering and testing spaces, aquaculture systems, small-boat and waterfront operations, educational and public-facing facilities, housing and critical infrastructure, ensuring safe and efficient operations and long-term alignment with the Institute’s research, education, and outreach missions. Recruit, develop, and retain outstanding faculty and staff and foster a collaborative environment that supports excellence, innovation, and entrepreneurship. Work collaboratively with the HBOI Faculty Assembly and other university stakeholders in the shared governance of the Institute. Serve on the Vice President for Research’s leadership team and contribute to the broader growth and direction of Florida Atlantic’s research enterprise. Represent HBOI and Florida Atlantic at national and international conferences, meetings, industry gatherings, and scientific and governmental forums. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and seven years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and nine years of appropriate experience required. Preferred Qualifications: Candidates must possess a doctoral degree in oceanography, marine science, engineering, biology, biotechnology, chemistry, aquaculture or another field relevant to the mission of Harbor Branch. Candidates should have significant senior-level leadership and management experience in a research-intensive university, research institute, government laboratory, industry research organization or comparable environment. Candidates must have or be able to obtain a Personnel Security Clearance (PCL). Strong candidates will demonstrate: • A distinguished record of scientific, engineering or research accomplishment and the professional stature necessary to lead a major research institute. • A sustained record of securing and managing significant public and/or private research funding. • Demonstrated experience developing substantive partnerships with industry, including sponsored research, technology development, testing, commercialization, joint initiatives or other collaborative programs. • A track record of cultivating relationships with senior executives, government leaders, federal agencies and other external partners. • Experience leading large, multidisciplinary research initiatives and building effective teams across organizational boundaries. • Demonstrated success growing research programs, developing new revenue sources and translating institutional assets and expertise into strategic partnerships. • Strong communication, interpersonal and relationship-building skills and the executive presence necessary to serve as the public face and leading advocate for HBOI. • Experience related to environmental and coastal science, marine ecosystem conservation, ocean technology, maritime systems, national defense, autonomous systems, marine science, biotechnology or other areas aligned with Florida Atlantic’s strategic research priorities is strongly preferred. Salary: Salary Commensurate with Experience Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Research Location: Harbor Branch (HBOI) Work Days and Hours: Monday-Friday some weekends Application Deadline: 2026-11-07 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Community-Coordinator_REQ22910": {
      "title": "Community Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Community Coordinator in Boca Raton, FL. The Community Coordinator supports students' success by fostering an inclusive and welcoming community where students feel a sense of belonging. This role helps develop and implement programs, initiatives, and engagement opportunities that promote student wellbeing, strengthen connections, and enhance the overall student experience. Summary of Responsibilities:   Interview, select, train, supervise, and evaluate a team of 8-14 Resident Assistants. Assist with implementing and assessing a residential curriculum. Contribute to a comprehensive assessment plan and utilize data to make evidence-based enhancements to programs and services. Actively recruit, advise, develop, and support the Community Council. Manage hall budgets for programming and supplies. Fiscally responsible for the use of a university purchasing card.  Assist with hall opening/closing procedures.  Advise students with personal and emotional conflicts and act as a referral agent for other campus resources. Provide follow-up and support student wellbeing. Administer Student Conduct process through adjudication of cases involving policy violations.  Interpret and ensure compliance with departmental and university policies, guidelines, and other relevant regulations. Educate staff and students to enforce policies. Serve as a customer service representative of the department and university. Maintain positive working relationships with custodians, maintenance specialists, and other facilities personnel.  Execute health and safety inspections for the residence hall. Review on-call reports and incident reports daily and provide necessary follow-up. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). ​ For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $51,500.00 - $53,045.00 Annually. Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP). College or Department: Student Affairs. Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm. Some evenings and weekends. Application Deadline: 2026-10-22 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Vice-President--Strategic-Philanthropy_REQ22938": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President, Strategic Philanthropy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks a deeply experienced, creative, and dynamic fundraiser to help lead a relationship-focused, results-oriented, donor-centered advancement team.   Florida Atlantic University, established in 1961, officially opened its doors in 1964 as Florida's fifth public university. Today, the University serves more than 30,000 undergraduate and graduate students across six campuses located along the southeast Florida coast and is ranked as a top public university by U.S. News and World Report.   FAU is an energetic and fast-growing institution, determined to propel itself to the forefront of innovation and scholarship. In recent years, the University has doubled its research expenditures and outpaced its peers in student achievement rates. Our students are bold, ambitious, and ready to take on the world.   Reporting directly to the Vice President of Institutional Advancement and CEO of the FAU Foundation and serving as a key member of the senior leadership team, the AVP of Strategic Philanthropy will lead the organization’s individual giving strategy while securing, stewarding, and growing major philanthropic investments that advance the mission of Florida Atlantic University’s Colleges and units.   In close partnership and collaboration with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, and the Assistant Vice President for Schools and Units, the school/college deans, and additional university leadership, the AVP will establish ambitious fundraising goals and develop performance metrics for development units and staff; driving efficiency and maximizing philanthropic support; utilize data analytics tools to identify trends and formulate strategies to drive the Advancement Officer metrics framework; work with Advancement Officer and campus partners to create and execute donor strategies; provide training and mentorship to fundraising staff; and maintain their own portfolio of high-level prospects. The AVP of Strategic Philanthropy works closely with Regionally assigned Directors of Advancement and will assist in developing and executing comprehensive strategies to identify, cultivate, solicit, and steward major gift donors, leadership donors, planned giving prospects, and campaign contributors. This position manages a portfolio of high-capacity donors and prospects while building a sustainable pipeline of philanthropic support to achieve annual and long-term fundraising goals.   The Assistant Vice President of Strategic Philanthropy is a valued member of the senior leadership team and will guide, coach, and supervise a team of Directors of Advancement focused on regional priorities, Legacy Giving, Foundation Relations, and Scholarships, and Student Affairs. This position will ensure the team meets philanthropic goals and works with committee members, volunteers, and community stakeholders to strengthen relationships and inspire transformational investments that support FAU’s mission. The successful candidate will experience a commitment to Advancement at the very top from the President; a seasoned, dynamic Vice President of Institutional Advancement with a winning track record; innovative and committed Provost and Deans; and the opportunities and responsibilities appropriate for fundraising leaders to complete Florida Atlantic’s next campaign.   Summary of Responsibilities: Provide strong leadership and guidance to a team of professionals, fostering a high-performance culture, including directly supervising a staff of 7, which includes: Regional Directors of Advancement (4) and an Assistant Scholarships & Student Affairs Director of Advancement Legacy Giving Executive Director and Associate Director Foundation Relations Executive Director and Assistant Director Set clear performance metrics, ensuring alignment with overall fundraising objectives, and conduct regular performance reviews. Strategically partner with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement and the Assistant Vice President for Schools and Units in all areas of fundraising, as well as preparing for a future campaign. Play a critical role in the development and execution of the University’s overall fundraising strategy, including partnering with the Vice President and other University leaders in setting goals, establishing strategies and plans, and assessing performance. Work collaboratively with the Assistant Vice President for Schools and Units, all Colleges, university leadership, units and programs, and advancement staff to creatively address and provide opportunities for donor-focused solicitations addressing donors’ holistic interests across the entirety of FAU; Serve as a collaborative peer and strategic thought partner to finance leadership regarding grants, contracts, budgets, and the formation of essential policies and procedures.   Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Characteristics: A leadership-level talent capable of overseeing and improving strategic regional major gift efforts, working effectively with ambitious teams, and contributing to a successful advancement and alumni relations operation. Collaborative, goal-oriented, strategic, and highly motivated working style. The ability to demonstrate leadership, take initiative, problem-solve, act independently and as a member of a team, successfully collaborate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize. The ability to demonstrate strategic thinking, good judgment, maturity, and personal integrity. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, and an ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with a diverse campus community including senior administrators, faculty, staff, and students, as well as donors, prospects, alumni, and community leaders. Ability to use tact and diplomacy to handle a broad range of high-level and sensitive situations with diverse personalities, and the ability to adeptly respond to challenges. Able to work beyond traditional work hours and on occasional holidays. Ability to travel as needed and adjust working hours to meet requirements of special tasks and events. Ability to translate academia-speak to diverse audiences. ​ FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A master's degree and at least 10 years of fundraising experience; A successful fundraising track record and strength in developing thoughtful and creative donor strategies in a complex organization; A deep knowledge and understanding of philanthropy and fundraising; Strong leadership skills and exceptional analytical and problem-solving skills; Demonstrable strength in developing thoughtful donor strategies, preferably in higher education; Progressive experience supervising and managing staff, budgets, and developing and implementing annual goals; Extensive experience managing and working with high-level donors with demonstrated measurable success; Experience in fundraising and capital campaigns; and Familiarity with fundraising software and analytical tools, as well as excellent verbal and written communication skills; Ability to successfully engage and motivate diverse groups of individuals at all levels, including staff, alumni, and volunteers; Familiarity with performance metrics and accountability measures and how to apply them to motivate and empower staff and educate stakeholders about the essentials of fundraising; Experience in strategic planning and a commitment to, and understanding of, the building steps for taking a research university’s advancement program to a new level of success; Ability to build trusting and productive relationships with the University’s leaders, colleagues, volunteers, donors, faculty, and staff; Demonstrated ability to develop cultivation and successful solicitation strategies across all university priorities, and the ability to acquire and creatively address donors’ interests and needs; Knowledge of university personnel policies and procedures is desirable; and Developing and implementing special events. Proficiency in using standard computer applications, including word-processing, spreadsheet, CRM software, calendaring, email, and online applications, and a working knowledge of social media. Raiser's Edge experience is helpful. Salary: $250,000 - $260,000. Annually Administrative, Managerial and Professional (AMP) FLSA Exempt College or Department: Division of Institutional Advancement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday. This position will require travel and/or work outside of standard business days and hours related to donor activities and engagement. Application Deadline: 2026-10-17 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This recruitment may close without prior notice ** APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Westgate/Licensed-Clinical-Social-Worker_REQ22883": {
      "title": "Licensed Clinical Social Worker",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Licensed Clinical Social Worker - Westgate, FL. The Licensed Clinical Social Worker (LCSW) provides therapy, crisis intervention, and case management while creating treatment plans based on patient assessments. The LCSW works with healthcare teams to deliver integrated care, ensure compliance with regulations, and maintain accurate records. Summary of Responsibilities Provide individual, family, and group psychotherapy to patients of all ages. Conduct biosocial assessments and develop individualized treatment plans. Provide individual psychotherapy sessions on a weekly or biweekly basis. Develop and modify treatment plans based on clinical progress and changing patient’s needs. Educate patients and families on mental health conditions and coping strategies. Use evidence-based therapeutic modalities such as CBT and DBT, motivational interviewing and trauma informed care. Works with substance use and addiction populations on an outpatient basis, serving substance use/dependency, active additions, court-ordered to attend local outpatient drug programs for individual and group therapy for those who have been arrested or are in current legal issues for DUIs, trafficking, DWI's or child custody cases related. Collaborate with medical providers, case managers, and other team members to support integrated care. Offer crisis intervention and risk assessments, including safety planning when necessary. Design and implement behavioral health programs aligned with the FQHC's mission, while monitoring outcomes and recommending enhancements based on patient and community needs. Assist patients in navigating social service systems, including housing, food security, and benefits access. Maintain timely, accurate, and confidential documentation in the electronic health record (EHR). Maintains patient scheduling level at 32 hours per week with average of 28 patients seen and 8 hours allocated for administrative time to assure note closure to be completed. Ensure compliance with all relevant federal, state, and local regulations, including HIPAA. Stay updated on trends, best practices, and behavioral health regulations to guide program improvements. Participate in audits, quality assurance reviews, care management meetings, and team discussions to uphold service standards. Support outreach to neighborhood schools/communities as directed. Participate in regular staff meetings, staff training programs, supervisory sessions, and accept the responsibility for aiding the development of positive team relationships as requested. Adhere to agency policy, procedures, and the professional code of ethics. Uphold ethical standards and best practices in line with NASW Code of Ethics and HIPAA regulations. Perform other ad hoc and job-related duties and projects as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $65,000.00 - $80,000.00 Annually. Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP). College or Department: College of Nursing. Location: Westgate Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:30 am - 5:00 pm. Application Deadline: 2026-10-05 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
