    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Director-of-Donor-Relations-and-Stewardship_REQ22927": {
      "title": "Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks a creative and motivated Advancement professional to fill a critical role on a relationship-focused, results-oriented, donor-centered advancement team. The Director of Donor Relations and Stewardship role requires a creative, thoughtful fundraising professional to design a comprehensive, meaningful acknowledgment and stewardship program for major and leadership gifts across the university. This role’s core responsibilities are to develop and execute an annual calendar of strategic donor relations deliverables, communications, and engagement opportunities (including a future Campaign) that show appreciation for support and inspire donors to give at higher levels. Summary of Responsibilities: Design and implement a comprehensive donor relations program, including; Define optimal donor journeys at established giving levels Create tools to facilitate meaningful and personalized donor experiences, including impact and stewardship reports, digital assets, etc. Implement a robust acknowledgment and stewardship program Develop targeted recognition opportunities for established donor levels Develop the voice for Florida Atlantic donor messaging, providing regular communication to the advancement team about University-wide milestones and happenings and ensuring the team receives updated presentation materials and email content Work collaboratively and effectively with Foundation leadership and advancement team members to create and implement individualized stewardship plans for major prospects; serve as a trusted advisor across the university programs to develop, manage and execute stewardship programs for donors Help train and educate Advancement and University staff on industry best practices in donor relations; work closely with staff across the University to instill and reinforce a culture of philanthropy Work collaboratively with the advancement communications team to develop corresponding materials; ensure all donor-facing materials align with overarching University communications and that materials complement and elevate donor stewardship Coordinate with the Director of Events and the Office of the President to ensure Foundation-wide event strategy aligns with the donor stewardship and communications calendars Expand and manage the acknowledgment process, ensuring gifts are thanked by the appropriate individual(s) in a timely manner and recorded in the database Continuously assess and adjust stewardship strategy as necessary to exceed donor expectations Manage and develop an effective team, providing effective communication, leadership by example, guidance and resources to staff; evaluate staff performance regularly and ensure staff team is appropriately and effectively supported Regularly report department performance, needs, and opportunities to the Assistant Vice President of Advancement Operations with quarterly updates to the AVP Schools and Units, AVP Strategic Philanthropy, and as needed, the VP of Institutional Advancement. Get creative, design stewardship and communications strategies that excite and engage our community across Colleges and programs! Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Characteristics: Collaborative, goal-oriented, strategic, and highly motivated working style. The ability to demonstrate leadership, take initiative, problem-solve, act independently and as a member of a team, successfully collaborate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize. The ability to demonstrate strategic thinking, good judgment, maturity, and personal integrity. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, and ability to craft compelling language to demonstrate program value and impact and to communicate and collaborate effectively with a diverse campus community including senior administrators, faculty, staff, and students, as well as donors, prospects, alumni, and community leaders. Ability to use tact and diplomacy to handle a broad range of high-level and sensitive situations with diverse personalities, and the ability to adeptly respond to challenges. Able to work beyond traditional work hours and on occasional holidays. Ability to travel as needed and adjust working hours to meet requirements of special tasks and events. Ability to translate academia-speak to diverse audiences.   FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of 7 years of experience in development, stewardship, events, and/or communications; experience directly supporting donor relations preferred. Ability to implement fundraising best practices while adapting for the uniqueness of the donor or program; experience in complex, multi-faceted organizations preferred. Regarded as a trusted expert internally in the field of donor relations and stewardship. Demonstrated success in managing a team towards achieving organizational goals. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously and prioritize responsibilities effectively. Collaborative team-player willing to work across departments to achieve the best possible results. Proficiency in using standard computer applications, including word-processing, spreadsheet, CRM software, calendaring, email, and online applications, and a working knowledge of social media. Raiser's Edge experience is helpful. Salary: $100,000 - $120,000. Annually Administrative, Managerial and Professional (AMP) FLSA Exempt College or Department: Division of Institutional Advancement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday. This position will require travel and/or work outside of standard business days and hours related to donor activities and engagement. Application Deadline: 2026-10-17 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This recruitment may close without prior notice ** APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Director-of-Advancement--College-of-Business_REQ22926": {
      "title": "Director of Advancement, College of Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks an experienced fundraising leader to join a relationship-focused, results-oriented, donor-centered advancement team. Opened in 1964, Florida Atlantic University serves more than 30,000 students across six beautiful campuses in South Florida. Among FAU’s 10 colleges is the College of Business, home to over 9,000 students, diverse academic departments, and an impressive offering of interdisciplinary and professional development programs taught by the college’s world-class faculty. Accredited by The Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business International (AACSB), the College of Business grants undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral degrees. FAU College of Business emphasizes innovation and entrepreneurism through practical instruction, real-life consulting opportunities, interaction with successful executives, and research efforts conducted at its variety of centers. Centers such as the Adams Center for Entrepreneurship; the Runway at Florida Atlantic; the Research Park at FAU; the WAVE Program; the Madden Center for Value Creation; and the Phil Smith Center for Free Enterprise all offer opportunities to create and test business models, create comprehensive business plans, and obtain external investments to fuel their start-ups. FAU Business has been recognized for outstanding institutional performance by organizations like U.S. News & World Report, The Princeton Review, Financial Times, and Bloomberg Businessweek. Strategically, the College strives to inspire students, faculty, and the regional business community to innovate and make fundamental and positive changes to the way business is conducted. The Director of Advancement for the College of Business at Florida Atlantic University works collaboratively with the Dean, Associate and Assistant Deans, and faculty, and under the supervision of the Vice President and/or an Assistant Vice President for Institutional Advancement. The Director plans, articulates, and implements a comprehensive strategic fundraising plan to meet the educational and research missions and activities of the College of Business and its programs and areas. The Director qualifies, cultivates, solicits, and stewards a portfolio of donors and prospective donors with the inclination and capacity to make significant gifts ($100,000 and greater) to the College of Business at FAU. The successful candidate will experience a commitment to Advancement at the very top from the President; a seasoned, dynamic Vice President of Institutional Advancement with a winning track record; an innovative and committed Dean at the College of Business; and the opportunities and responsibilities appropriate for fundraising leaders to complete Florida Atlantic’s next campaign. Summary of Responsibilities: Develop and implement comprehensive cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship strategies for individual major, legacy, and principal gift prospects assigned. Work both independently and in concert with Institutional Advancement colleagues to implement strategies leading to direct solicitation of gifts of $100,000 and more. Build a strong pipeline of alumni and other prospective donors to expand the portfolio of qualified prospects for gifts of $100,000 and more. Create and execute solicitation and closure strategies for major gifts aligned with the College of Business and University fundraising priorities and campaigns, measured against the attainment of personal metrics associated with the position. Collaborate with the Dean, department chairs, and faculty to identify funding priorities, assess relevance and feasibility for proposed project/priority, and develop and manage comprehensive strategies to secure gifts for selected priorities. Devise individualized involvement/engagement strategies for all prospects using an approach that ensures that most highly rated prospects receive the most attention. Partner with Institutional Advancement’s Legacy Giving Office to devise an overall strategy for cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding planned gift donors. In concert with Institutional Advancement colleagues, oversee the preparation of necessary materials including concept papers, funding proposals, briefings for FAU leadership and board members when necessary, and scheduled stewardship reports, for all assigned prospects. Identify prospects to participate on boards, committees, or other programs that promote the cultivation process. Partner with the Donor Relations and Stewardship Office to ensure appropriate stewardship is provided to donors on existing endowment and current-use funds. Facilitate effective communication between the College of Business and its Centers and programs, and the division of Institutional Advancement. Participate in signature events at the University, within the College, and in the community that provide opportunities for strategic engagement with prospects and donors. Manage the advancement/fundraising function of the College of Business Advisory Board; act as a liaison to the Board and to the Office of Institutional Advancement on policies, procedures, and approvals. In conjunction with the College’s scholarship contacts, oversee that all donor outcomes related to scholarships, such as thank-you notes, event attendance, and in-person visits, are executed in a timely manner. Participate in weekly meetings with the Dean to discuss donors and other fundraising priorities with the College of Business. Supervise a team of advancement and community engagement colleagues in the College of Business. Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Characteristics: Collaborative, goal-oriented, strategic, and highly motivated working style. The ability to demonstrate leadership, take initiative, problem-solve, act independently and as a member of a team, successfully collaborate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize. The ability to demonstrate strategic thinking, good judgment, maturity, and personal integrity. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, and an ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with a diverse campus community including senior administrators, faculty, staff, and students, as well as donors, prospects, alumni, and community leaders. Ability to use tact and diplomacy to handle a broad range of high-level and sensitive situations with diverse personalities, and the ability to adeptly respond to challenges. Able to work beyond traditional work hours and on occasional holidays. Ability to travel as needed and adjust working hours to meet requirements of special tasks and events. Ability to translate academia-speak to diverse audiences. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree and seven years of fundraising experience, or a master’s degree and five years of fundraising experience, is required. Able to demonstrate measurable success in closing gifts ($100,000 or more) from individual donors, including alumni and friends, and/or institutional donors such as foundations and corporations. Demonstrable experience developing fundraising strategies in partnership with senior academic leadership. Proficiency in using standard computer applications, including word-processing, spreadsheet, CRM software, calendaring, email, and online applications, and a working knowledge of social media. Raiser's Edge experience is helpful. Salary: $165,000 - $180,000. Annually Administrative, Managerial and Professional (AMP) FLSA Exempt College or Department: Division of Institutional Advancement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday. This position will require travel and/or work outside of standard business days and hours related to donor activities and engagement. Application Deadline: 2026-10-17 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This recruitment may close without prior notice ** APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Director-of-Advancement--College-of-Medicine_REQ22924": {
      "title": "Director of Advancement, College of Medicine",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University seeks an experienced fundraising leader to join a relationship-focused, results-oriented, donor-centered advancement team. The Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is one of the nation's fastest-growing medical schools. We are committed to our core missions of advancing excellence in education and training, research, clinical care, and community engagement.  We are embarking on a bold transformation to evolve from our strong foundation as a community-based medical school into a leading academic health system that advances healthcare through excellence in our core missions. The Director of Advancement for the Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University works collaboratively with the Dean, Associate and Assistant Deans, and faculty, and under the supervision of the Vice President and/or an Assistant Vice President for Institutional Advancement. The Director plans, articulates, and implements a comprehensive strategic fundraising plan to meet the core missions of the Schmidt College of Medicine and its departments, programs, and areas. The Director qualifies, cultivates, solicits, and stewards a portfolio of donors and prospective donors with the inclination and capacity to make significant gifts ($100,000 and greater) to the Schmidt College of Medicine at FAU. The successful candidate will join an institution with a commitment to Advancement at the very top from the President; a seasoned, dynamic Vice President of Institutional Advancement with a winning track record; an innovative Dean committed to philanthropy; and the opportunities and responsibilities appropriate for fundraising leaders to complete Florida Atlantic’s next campaign. Summary of Responsibilities: Develop and implement comprehensive cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship strategies for individual major, legacy, and principal gift prospects assigned. Work both independently and in concert with Institutional Advancement colleagues to implement strategies leading to direct solicitation of gifts of $100,000 and more. Build a strong pipeline of alumni and other prospective donors to expand the portfolio of qualified prospects for gifts of $100,000 and more. Create and execute solicitation and closure strategies for major gifts aligned with the Schmidt College of Medicine and University fundraising priorities and campaigns, measured against the attainment of personal metrics associated with the position. Collaborate with the Dean, department chairs, and faculty to identify funding priorities, assess relevance and feasibility for proposed project/priority, and develop and manage comprehensive strategies to secure gifts for selected priorities. Devise individualized involvement/engagement strategies for all prospects using an approach that ensures that most highly rated prospects receive the most attention. Partner with Institutional Advancement’s Legacy Giving Office to devise an overall strategy for cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding planned gift donors. In concert with Institutional Advancement colleagues, oversee the preparation of necessary materials including concept papers, funding proposals, briefings for FAU leadership and board members when necessary, and scheduled stewardship reports, for all assigned prospects. Identify prospects to participate on boards, committees, or other programs that promote the cultivation process. Partner with the Donor Relations and Stewardship Office to ensure appropriate stewardship is provided to donors on existing endowment and current-use funds. Facilitate effective communication between the Schmidt College of Medicine and the division of Institutional Advancement. Participate in signature events at the University, within the College, and in the community that provide opportunities for strategic engagement with prospects and donors. Manage the advancement/fundraising function of the Schmidt College of Medicine Advisory Board; act as a liaison to the Board and to the Office of Institutional Advancement on policies, procedures, and approvals. In conjunction with the College’s scholarship contacts, oversee that all donor outcomes related to scholarships, such as thank-you notes, event attendance, and in-person visits, are executed in a timely manner. Participate in weekly meetings with the Dean to discuss donors and other fundraising priorities with the Schmidt College of Medicine. Supervise and support a team of advancement and community engagement professionals in the Schmidt College of Medicine responsible for fundraising, donor engagement, and strategic initiatives.​ Successful Candidate Will Have the Following Characteristics: Collaborative, goal-oriented, strategic, and highly motivated working style. The ability to demonstrate leadership, take initiative, problem-solve, act independently and as a member of a team, successfully collaborate, handle multiple tasks simultaneously, and prioritize. The ability to demonstrate strategic thinking, good judgment, maturity, and personal integrity. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, and an ability to communicate and collaborate effectively with a diverse campus community including senior administrators, faculty, staff, and students, as well as donors, prospects, alumni, and community leaders. Ability to use tact and diplomacy to handle a broad range of high-level and sensitive situations with diverse personalities, and the ability to adeptly respond to challenges. Able to work beyond traditional work hours and on occasional holidays. Ability to travel as needed and adjust working hours to meet requirements of special tasks and events. Ability to communicate complex academic and research priorities in ways that resonate with potential donors. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree and seven years of fundraising experience, or a master’s degree and five years of fundraising experience, is required. Able to demonstrate measurable success in closing gifts ($100,000 or more) from individual donors, including alumni and friends, and/or institutional donors such as foundations and corporations. Demonstrable experience developing fundraising strategies in partnership with senior academic leadership. Proficiency in using standard computer applications, including word-processing, spreadsheet, CRM software, calendaring, email, and online applications, and a working knowledge of social media. Raiser's Edge experience is helpful. Salary: $165,000 - $180,000. Annually Administrative, Managerial and Professional (AMP) FLSA Exempt College or Department: Division of Institutional Advancement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday. This position will require travel and/or work outside of standard business days and hours related to donor activities and engagement. Application Deadline: 2026-10-17 Special Instructions to Applicant: **This recruitment may close without prior notice ** APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
