    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Urologist---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor_REQ21636": {
      "title": "Urologist - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The FAU Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine seeks a dynamic and collaborative Urologist to join our clinical faculty at the rank of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor. The successful candidate will be a highly skilled and specialized medical professional responsible for the diagnosis, treatment, and management of diseases and conditions of the urinary tract and male reproductive system. This position offers the opportunity to provide exemplary, compassionate care within the Florida Atlantic Medical Group with a strong emphasis on serving our broad-based patient populations and actively engaging in teaching, mentorship, and scholarly activities within a thriving community-based medical school setting. The mission of the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine is to advance the health and well-being of our community through educating and training the next generation of physicians - medical students, residents, and fellows - who will thrive as lifelong learners and compassionate, skilled practitioners. Our programs are built on a foundation of evidence-based, patient-centered care and are enriched by a culture of innovation, mentorship, and scholarly growth. Faculty at the Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine benefit from close collaboration across medical specialties and strong partnerships with both community-based and academic healthcare providers, creating a dynamic environment to advance excellence in education, clinical care, and research. We are looking for someone with an innovative spirit and a passion for advancing scientific knowledge and healthcare delivery. Responsibilities: Clinical Care Provide comprehensive diagnostic, medical, and surgical management for patients with urologic conditions including kidney, bladder, prostate, adrenal, and male reproductive disorders, with a focus on improving urological health outcomes. Perform diagnostic and therapeutic urologic procedures. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams to ensure safe and coordinated care. Participate in hospital and community-based outreach programs to expand access to urological healthcare. Research & Scholarship Engage in clinical research, quality improvement, or public health initiatives related to urology. Share scholarly efforts through conference presentations and peer-reviewed publications. Service & Community Engagement Serve on departmental, college, and university committees. Collaborate with local agencies and community organizations to improve urological healthcare delivery and outcomes. Contribute to institutional initiatives aimed at advancing clinical care and community education. Academic Teaching & Mentorship As this is a primarily clinical position, teaching and mentorship are not requirements of the position at this time, however, there may be future opportunities to: provide high-quality teaching to medical students, residents, and fellows in clinical and didactic settings. mentor learners in patient care, clinical reasoning, research methodology, and professional development. contribute to curriculum development with emphasis on evidence-based practice and urological healthcare. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited institution and credentials that merit appointment at the rank of assistant professor or higher required. • A Florida medical license, or the ability to obtain one, and ABMS Board certification or eligibility in Urology required. • Demonstrated commitment to academic teaching, scholarship, and community engagement. Preferred Competencies • Evidence of multidisciplinary and interprofessional collaboration. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-10-16 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Nursing-Adjuncts_REQ21767": {
      "title": "Nursing Adjuncts",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-14\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The College of Nursing (CON) seeks qualified Nursing Adjuncts to support the teaching mission of the college by providing high-quality instruction in classroom, laboratory, simulation, and/or clinical settings. Adjuncts are part-time instructional professionals who bring current clinical expertise to the learning environment and support the preparation of future nurses through teaching, mentoring, and evaluation of students. Adjuncts will contribute to the college’s caring-based educational philosophy by fostering a supportive and engaging learning environment for students. Responsibilities may include teaching undergraduate nursing courses, supervising clinical practice experiences, evaluating student performance, maintaining course materials in the learning management system, and collaborating with course coordinators and program leadership to ensure course objectives and accreditation standards are met. The College of Nursing is known for its commitment to caring science and preparing nurses who are competent, compassionate, and responsive to the health needs of various communities. Adjuncts support this mission by bringing real-world clinical practice into the academic setting and helping students integrate theory with professional nursing practice. Minimum Qualifications: o Baccalaureate degree in nursing (BSN) from an accredited institution, five years of experience in nursing, and certification in clinical area of teaching; or Master’s degree in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution o Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license o Minimum of two years of professional nursing practice experience in the specialty area relevant to the teaching assignment Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Christine E. Lynn College of Nursing Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2027-01-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: o CV o Copy of current RN licensure o Official transcript o 2 letters of reference o Copy of current malpractice insurance coverage o Copy of current CPR certification Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Harbor-Branch-HBOI/Postdoctoral-Fellow-Application-of-Machine-Learning-and-Robotics_REQ21771": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow Application of Machine Learning and Robotics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-25\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University's Systems and Imaging Laboratory (SAIL) at Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute in Fort Pierce, FL, is seeking a 12-month, non-tenure Postdoctoral Fellow position. Extension of the appointment beyond one year is possible, depending on funding availability and performance. This position will focus on developing robotics and cyber physical systems solutions using machine learning and artificial intelligence to support different aspects of marine science, with opportunities to expand to other areas. Currently, SAIL is conducting multiple projects ranging from Hybrid Aerial Underwater Robotic System (HAUCS)– a cyber physical system (CPS) for aquaculture, to sensors and platforms for maritime applications. In this position, your primary task will be to lead the development of algorithms, software, and hardware to extend the current HAUCS framework. This includes developing the sensors, sensing robotic platforms, environmental prediction models, and visualization tools as needed. Additional tasks include field experiments to test the instruments and validate models; preparing data reports and presentations for technical conferences; publishing results in peer-reviewed journals; and mentoring students and junior scientists. There will also be opportunities to work on other related projects, including the application of AI to solve underwater vision problems and Phase III of the Next Generation Sensor Systems for Natural Oceanic Bioluminescence Assessments. The Postdoctoral Fellow will be able to grow his/her skills in research and grant writing by taking an active role in identifying funding opportunities and developing grant proposals. Minimum Qualifications: - A doctorate (foreign equivalent acceptable) in electrical engineering, computer science, engineering, or related area. - A team player who is willing to train junior scientists in the lab. - Expertise in robotics and unmanned aerial vehicle development, in particular electronic hardware design and embedded system development. - Comprehension of common machine learning algorithms and image analysis. - Independent, self-motivated, well-organized, and critical thinker. - Good written and verbal communication skills. Salary: $55,000.00 - $65,000.00 College or Department: Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute/Systems and Imaging Lab (SAIL) Location: Harbor Branch (HBOI) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of interest, transcripts, and contact information for three professional references including email addresses and phone numbers. Transcripts: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Professor-of-Teaching_REQ22102": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Teaching",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-14\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Department of Civil, Environmental & Geomatics Engineering ( http://www.cege.fau.edu/ ) at Florida Atlantic University welcomes applications for a non-tenure-track Assistant Teaching Professor position in Civil, Environmental and Geomatics Engineering. The department is particularly interested in a candidate who holds a Professional Engineer (P.E.) license and whose expertise in civil and environmental engineering includes significant design experience in the preparation of plans, specifications, and engineering studies. Candidates whose academic work focuses on applied, industry-relevant transportation problems or emerging analytical methods in the field are strongly encouraged to apply. The position is expected to teach structural analysis, drawings classes, and design-related classes including senior design capstone. The Department of Civil, Environmental & Geomatics Engineering ( CEGE ) hosts 3 ABET-accredited undergraduate programs, a Master’s degree in Civil Engineering, and a Ph.D. in Transportation and Environmental Engineering with about 400 undergraduate and 100 graduate students. The faculty is highly interdisciplinary and conducts research primarily in the broad thematic areas of Urban Mobility, Infrastructure, and Sustainability/Resilience. The Department has three research centers: the Center for Infrastructure and Constructed Facilities ( fau.edu/engineering/cege/research/cicf/ ), the Center for Water Resiliency and Risk Reduction ( cwr3.fau.edu ), and the Freight Mobility Research Institute ( fmri.fau.edu ).   The FAU College of Engineering and Computer Science is in the top three fastest progressing engineering colleges in the nation (US News and World Report Rankings 2020-2022). The college offers degrees with a modern twist that bear specializations in areas of national priority such as artificial intelligence, cybersecurity, internet-of-things, transportation and supply chain management, and data science. For more information about the college, please visit eng.fau.edu . Florida Atlantic University, established in 1961, officially opened its doors in 1964 as the fifth public university in Florida. Today, the university serves more than 31,000 undergraduate and graduate students across six campuses located along the southeast Florida coast. In recent years, the university has doubled its research expenditure and outpaced its peers in student achievement rates. FAU is ranked as a top 100 public university by U.S. News & World Report. In 2025, the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education designated Florida Atlantic as R1: Very High Research Spending and Doctorate Production – the most prestigious research accolade in the country. For more information about FAU, visit  www.fau.edu . Appointments are expected to start in Fall 2026. Minimum Qualifications: • Applicants must have a B.S. degree and a Ph.D. in civil or environmental engineering or a closely related engineering discipline, with a Professional Engineer (P.E.) license in the State of Florida, or in another state with the ability to acquire such a license in Florida. • Demonstrated ability in communication, interpersonal skills, collaboration, leadership, and student motivation are required attributes. • Expected to teach and mentor graduate and undergraduate students and to participate in professional and departmental service activities. • Candidates are expected to become familiar with new pedagogies such as active learning and AI literacy in civil and environmental engineering, including re-creating knowledge for educating and nurturing students and translating knowledge into practice. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: College of Engineering and Computer Science Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following in PDF format: a letter of interest that incorporates research and teaching statements, an up-to-date CV, and names of three references. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Graduate-Nursing-Adjuncts_REQ21774": {
      "title": "Graduate Nursing Adjuncts",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-20\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU on its race to excellence. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Christine E. Lynn College of Nursing at Florida Atlantic University invites applications for Graduate Nursing Adjuncts to support the Master of Science in Nursing (MSN), and Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP). Adjuncts are part-time instructional professionals who contribute specialized expertise in advanced nursing practice and support the academic preparation of graduate nursing students. Graduate adjuncts may teach didactic, clinical, laboratory, or online courses and collaborate with course coordinators and program leadership to ensure alignment with program outcomes, accreditation standards, and evidence-based nursing practice. Responsibilities include facilitating student learning, evaluating student performance, maintaining course materials within the university’s learning management system, and providing guidance and mentorship to graduate nursing students. Adjuncts are expected to support the College’s caring-based philosophy and integrate clinical expertise, scholarship, and professional experience into the educational environment. The College is internationally recognized for its commitment to caring science—expanding the science of caring, practicing the art of nursing, studying its meaning, and living it in academic and clinical practice. Adjunct appointments are part-time and assigned per course, per semester, based on program needs and enrollment. Typical Responsibilities Supervise and evaluate graduate nursing students in advanced practice clinical settings Teach graduate nursing courses in classroom, online, simulation, or clinical environments Collaborate with course coordinators and faculty to ensure consistency in course delivery and student learning outcomes  Evaluate student assignments, clinical performance, and competencies  Maintain accurate course records, grades, and student evaluations  Participate in adjunct orientation and comply with university and college policies  Provide mentorship and professional guidance to students preparing for advanced nursing roles Minimum Qualifications: o MSN degree/post-graduate certificate in an area of advanced practice specialty and three years of experience working as an advanced practice nurse in area of specialty (Clinical adjunct positions only) o National certification as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) or specialty certification where appropriate o Current, unencumbered Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) or Registered Nurse (RN) license in Florida (or eligibility for licensure) Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Christine E. Lynn College of Nursing Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-12-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: o CV o Copy of current RN licensure o Official transcript from master's program (doctoral program, if applicable) o 2 letters of reference o Copy of current malpractice insurance coverage o Copy of current CPR certification Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Director-for-Student-Staff-Learning-and-Development_REQ22972": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Student Staff Learning and Development",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Assistant Director for Student Staff Learning and Development. - Boca Raton, FL. The Assistant Director of Student Staff Learning and Development serves on the Residential Education leadership team within the Department of Housing and Residential Education. This live-in position provides strategic leadership for the learning and development of more than 225 Resident Assistants, Front Desk Staff, and seasonal student employees across the Boca Raton and Jupiter campuses, while supporting the recruitment and selection of student staff. This position requires living on campus in a provided furnished apartment. The Department of Housing and Residential Education’s residential facilities do not close. We serve our students and remain open during all campus holidays and closures. Due to our 12-month operation, staff will work on-call hours when the University is closed or when classes are not in session (ex. during Thanksgiving, Winter Break, and Spring Break). This position is considered an essential employee. In severe weather or emergency situations, the University may suspend classes or close the University. This position would be expected to remain at or report to their facilities as soon as conditions reasonably permit . Summary of responsibilities: Student Staff Recruitment and Selectio n Provide strategic leadership for the recruitment and selection of Resident Assistants, Front Desk Staff, and seasonal student staff across the Boca Raton and Jupiter campuses. Develop and continuously improve recruitment strategies, timelines, and selection processes that attract qualified student staff candidates and support departmental staffing needs. Coordinate major recruitment and selection initiatives. Develop recruitment strategies and processes for off-cycle positions, including Winter Break Staff, Camps and Conferences, and other seasonal student staff positions. Lead the Recruitment and Selection Committee and engage professional and student staff in recruitment and selection efforts. Collaborate with departmental HR partners to ensure student staff recruitment and employment processes align with university policies and applicable requirements. Evaluate recruitment outcomes and selection processes and utilize data and feedback to identify opportunities for continuous improvement. Student Staff Learning and Development Provide strategic leadership for the department's student staff learning and development philosophy. Lead the development and implementation of a comprehensive, competency-based student staff learning and development model aligned with the department's residential curriculum and informed by industry standards. Design and facilitate intentional learning experiences that prepare student staff to support student learning, engagement, community development, wellbeing, and student success. Develop and implement pre-semester training, in-service education, and ongoing professional development opportunities for student staff. Develop a tiered learning approach that considers differences in student staff experience, responsibilities, and developmental needs. Coordinate a year-round In-Service Training Calendar that supports continued learning, skill development, reflection, professional growth, and career readiness. Collaborate with campus partners and subject-matter experts to develop and facilitate educational experiences that support departmental and student learning goals. Provide onboarding and learning support for student staff hired outside of standard training cycles. Lead the Learning and Development Committee and foster shared responsibility for student staff learning and development across the department. Assess student staff learning and development initiatives and utilize assessment findings and participant feedback to inform future planning and program improvement. Student Staff Experience, Performance, and Engagement Provide leadership for the student staff experience from recruitment and onboarding through ongoing development, performance, and transition. Develop and continuously improve systems that support student staff engagement, belonging, accountability, and success. Develop and oversee student staff performance evaluation and accountability processes. Provide guidance and support to Residential Education supervisors regarding student staff performance, coaching, documentation, and performance improvement. Establish clear expectations and resources that promote consistent approaches to student staff supervision, coaching, recognition, and development. Maintain and update student staff job descriptions, employment agreements, evaluation tools, and related resources. Monitor student staff records and assignments within Workday, StarRez, and other departmental systems to support accurate staffing and supervision. Utilize student staff feedback, assessment data, industry publications, and departmental priorities to identify opportunities to strengthen the student staff experience. Develop strategies that support student staff engagement, leadership development, retention, and continued professional growth. Advise the National Residence Hall Honorary (NRHH), a national honor society and recognition branch of the National Association of College and University Residence Halls. Incident Response and Risk Management Participate in the departmental second-level on-call rotation and provide after-hours leadership, consultation, and support. Provide leadership and decision-making during critical incidents and emergency situations involving student staff, student welfare, facilities, or conduct concerns. Guide professional and student staff in responding to incidents and following established university and departmental protocols. Support appropriate follow-up, documentation, referrals, and communication following significant incidents. Provide consultation and support to professional staff and student staff navigating complex or high-risk situations. As an essential employee, remain on-site or report to campus during university closures, holidays, and critical incidents as required. Administrative and Operational Oversight Oversee administrative systems and processes related to student staff recruitment, employment, onboarding, learning, evaluation, and development. Maintain accurate student staff records and documentation in Workday, StarRez, and other departmental systems. Develop and maintain student staff resources, procedures, timelines, and communication materials that support consistent departmental practices. Monitor student staff staffing levels, recruitment outcomes, training participation, and other relevant data to inform planning and decision-making. Utilize departmental resources responsibly and contribute to budget planning related to student staff recruitment, learning, and development. Recommend improvements to departmental policies, procedures, and systems that strengthen the student staff experience and support departmental priorities. Collaborate with Residential Education leadership to promote consistency in student staff expectations, supervision, learning, and development across the department.   Campus Engagement Provide operational and programmatic support for university-wide events, including Orientation, Family Weekend, Admissions initiatives, athletic events, and campus traditions. Serve on departmental committees and represent Residential Education on divisional or university committees as assigned. Develop collaborative partnerships with campus departments and stakeholders that strengthen student staff learning, development, and engagement. Maintain engagement with professional associations and current practices related to residential education, student staff learning and development, student learning, and higher education. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).    For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and four years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $61,000 - $63,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs: Housing & Residential Education Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday-Friday,8am - 5pm. Must be available to work weekends and nights. Application Deadline: 2026-10-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Intramural-Sports-Official_REQ23031": {
      "title": "Intramural Sports Official",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nPart time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking multiple Intramural Sports Officials. - Boca Raton, FL. Summary of responsibilities: Officiate designated Intramural Sports (average of 2 nights per week) Ability to score keep designated sports Ensure security of participants, spectators, facility, & equipment Assist the Sport Programs Supervisor with pre and post-game logistics and administrative functions Assist the Sport Programs Supervisor with checking in teams and verifying eligibility Professionally and proactively assist participants with disputes and minor problems Providing positive public relations, program promotion, and policy education to staff & participants Assist with emergency situations and evacuations, as they arise Manage game equipment Perform other duties as assigned. Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | B DB Minimum Qualifications: FAU degree-seeking undergraduate student with a minimum of six credit hours (or twelve if international) and a 2.0 GPA required. Salary: $15 hourly. Temporary Student College or Department: Division of Student Affairs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Sunday, 8am - 5pm. Up to 20 hours per week. Application Deadline: 2026-10-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: This is a part time position. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Purchasing-Agent-III_REQ23043": {
      "title": "Purchasing Agent III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Division of Financial Affairs at Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Purchasing Agent III in Boca Raton, FL. The Purchasing Agent III is responsible for developing, coordinating, and executing strategic procurement and contracting activities in support of the University community. Provides comprehensive procurement services throughout the procurement and contract lifecycle, ensuring compliance with Florida State University System Board of Governors (BOG) regulations, applicable procurement regulations and policies, and all relevant federal, state, and local laws. Promotes effective competition, cost efficiency, risk mitigation, contract compliance, and best value through sound procurement strategies, market research, financial analysis, and supplier relationship management. Serves as a procurement advisor and strategic partner to University departments, supporting institutional objectives through transparent, accountable, and results-oriented procurement practices. Summary of Responsibilities: Strategic Procurement and Stakeholder Engagement Develops, coordinates, and executes procurement strategies for assigned spend categories and commodities in alignment with University priorities, operational requirements, and applicable regulatory frameworks. Collaborates with departments across the Division of Financial Affairs and the broader University community to assess procurement needs, establish sourcing strategies, evaluate alternatives, and develop solutions that achieve operational objectives and deliver best value. Serves as a procurement liaison and advisor to end-user departments, project managers, and other stakeholders, providing guidance on procurement policies, procedures, competitive requirements, contracting options, and applicable BOG regulations and state statutes. Manages multiple procurement initiatives concurrently in a fast-paced, service-oriented environment, balancing competing priorities, project milestones, regulatory requirements, and established deadlines.   Procurement Lifecycle and Competitive Solicitations Coordinates and supports the full procurement lifecycle, from initial requirements assessment and sourcing strategy through solicitation, evaluation, award, contract execution, and ongoing contract administration. Develops, coordinates, and administers competitive solicitation documents, including Invitations to Negotiate (ITNs), Requests for Proposals (RFPs), and Invitations to Bid (ITBs), ensuring requirements are clearly defined, evaluation methodologies are appropriate, and solicitation processes comply with applicable regulations and University policies. Conducts market research and supplier outreach to identify qualified sources, assess market conditions, evaluate available solutions, and promote effective competition.  Analyzes and evaluates procurement alternatives, including state, county, cooperative, and other authorized public-sector contract vehicles, to identify compliant sourcing opportunities and maximize institutional value. Participates in bid and proposal evaluations, conducts cost comparisons and financial analyses, assesses supplier responses, and develops recommendations based on documented evaluation criteria, operational requirements, compliance considerations, and overall value to the University. Contract Development and Administration Coordinates the review, negotiation, routing, execution, and modification of supplier contracts, purchase orders, and change orders in accordance with University policies, delegated authority, and applicable regulatory requirements. Supports contract administration and management throughout the contract term, including monitoring contract expenditures, purchase order balances, invoice activity, deliverables, renewal provisions, expiration dates, and other critical contractual milestones. Collaborate with end-user departments, Accounts Payable, project stakeholders, and other relevant units to resolve contract-related issues, address supplier performance concerns, and promote timely and accurate invoice processing. Assists in the resolution of supplier disputes, contractual discrepancies, performance issues, and other procurement-related matters, escalating issues as appropriate to protect the University’s interests. Maintains accurate and complete procurement documentation to support transparency, accountability, internal controls, and audit readiness. Compliance, Risk Management, and Operational Effectiveness Interprets and applies applicable BOG regulations, state statutes, University procurement policies, and other relevant requirements to procurement and contracting activities. Identifies potential compliance gaps, contractual risks, process deficiencies, and opportunities to strengthen procurement controls; recommends appropriate corrective actions and risk mitigation strategies. Promotes consistent application of procurement requirements and supports the development of compliant, defensible, and well-documented procurement decisions. Utilizes the Workday enterprise resource planning (ERP) system and other designated procurement technologies to facilitate procurement transactions, maintain accurate records, monitor contract activity, and support effective workflow management. Prepares, analyzes, and interprets reports related to procurement activity, contract utilization, expenditures, spend patterns, supplier performance, and operational trends to support informed decision-making and continuous improvement. Customer Service and Organizational Support Provides professional, responsive, and solutions-oriented service to University departments, suppliers, and other stakeholders while maintaining the integrity of procurement policies and established controls. Communicates procurement requirements, timelines, procedures, and decisions clearly and effectively to stakeholders with varying levels of procurement knowledge. Identifies opportunities to streamline workflows, improve procurement practices, strengthen internal controls, and enhance service delivery. Provides cross-functional support and serves as a backup for other Procurement functions to maintain operational continuity and meet departmental needs. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).    For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of relevant professional experience. Demonstrated experience in procurement and contracting, including competitive solicitations, contract development and administration, supplier negotiations, sourcing analysis, and supplier relationship management. Knowledge of procurement principles, competitive purchasing practices, contract management, and regulatory compliance requirements. Demonstrated analytical, problem-solving, organizational, and project management skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet established deadlines. Strong written and verbal communication, stakeholder engagement, negotiation, and customer service skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and PowerPoint. Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience in public higher education procurement Experience developing and administering complex competitive solicitations, including ITNs, RFPs, and ITBs. Experience with Euna Solutions/Bonfire or comparable electronic public procurement and solicitation platforms. Experience with Workday ERP or comparable enterprise procurement and financial management systems. Familiarity with Florida public-sector procurement requirements, including applicable BOG regulations, state statutes, and University procurement policies. Experience conducting market research, cost and pricing analyses, supplier evaluations, contract utilization reviews, and procurement reporting. Demonstrated ability to identify procurement risks, strengthen internal controls, improve processes, and support audit-ready documentation. Experience with strategic procurement and contracting activities for facilities management, physical plant, construction, and housing initiatives. Required Licenses, Certifications, and/or Other Specific Requirements of Law: Valid driver’s license required. Subject to a criminal background check, which may include Level II screening in accordance with Florida Statute §435.04. Position is subject to applicable federal and state privacy regulations. Salary: $58,000.00 - $80,000.00 Commensurate with experience College or Department: Division of Financial Affairs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m Application Deadline: 2026-10-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Academic-Advisor-III_REQ22589": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The College of Social Work & Criminal Justice at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Academic Advisor III in Boca Raton, FL. The Academic Advisor III serves as a dedicated partner in student success, providing holistic academic advising and guidance to students throughout their educational journey. Through proactive outreach, degree planning, graduation support, and collaboration with university partners, this role helps students navigate academic requirements, achieve their educational goals, and persist to graduation. The position also supports recruitment, retention, and student engagement initiatives while contributing to a welcoming and student-centered advising environment. *The primary work location for this position is the Boca Raton campus. This role will also require travel to—and work at—Davie campus. Summary of Responsibilities: Serve as an academic advisor in providing academic advising and program guidance to CDSI students.  Assist all CDSI students on the Broward Campuses through the academic process from initial contact to graduation.   Assist students with exploring and gathering information on University and College policies, procedures and degree requirements.  Direct to the appropriate University office for assistance with concerns that do not fall within the purview of the CAC.  Maintain the college academic files for students in relevant college degree programs.   Serves as liaison with the Veterans office and be primary advisor for all active-duty military or veterans. Reinforce and support student degree progress, academic success, and retention, in alignment with the strategic priorities of the college and its ongoing commitment to student success. Help create and sustain a positive environment in which all students have access to high-quality advising. Serve as an academic advisor to all Social Work and Criminal Justice (SW-CJ) students through the academic process from initial contact to graduation. Assist students with exploring and gathering information on University and College policies, procedures, and degree requirements. Serve as liaison to the BSW field practicum education team, confirm that BSW majors are eligible and meet the criteria to apply for the practicum course (SOW4510), monitor progress in spreadsheet, enter permission for students to register for SOW4510. Process applications for degree and conduct graduation checks. Manage online  queue for change of majors,  or  minors by approving or denying requests. Serve as liaison to the Veterans office and be primary advisor for all active-duty military or veterans. Maintain up-to-date knowledge about the College’s programs and requirements. Advise students about the courses and requirements for degree programs. Inform students about possible consequences of academic decisions (e.g., adding, dropping, withdrawing, changing major, repeated attempts). Educate students about course planning and registration processes. Make appropriate referrals to students perceived as at-risk and act as an advocate for student success. Monitor student academic plans to provide timely, proactive outreach to ensure degree progression and timely graduation. Direct students to the appropriate university office for assistance with concerns that do not fall within the purview of SW-CJ Advising Services. Support Advising Services with student programming and special events. Participate in student recruitment and orientation presentations. Maintain college academic files for students in relevant college degree programs. Recognize the importance of key performance indicators and work competently with available software and technology to facilitate timely and data-driven advising. Work collaboratively with multiple units across the university. Perform other job-related duties as assigned.  FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).   For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and three years of appropriate experience required. Preferred Qualifications/Skills: Appreciative Advisor Certification is strongly preferred. Salary: $62,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: College of Social Work & Criminal Justice: Advising Services Operations Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, with four days scheduled from 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. and one designated day each week from 9:30 a.m. - 6 p.m. *The primary work location for this position is the Boca Raton campus. This role will also require travel to—and work at—Davie campus. Application Deadline: 2026-10-29 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Clinical---Off-Campus-Location-COM-use-only/Director--Surgical-Simulation-and-Technology--Assistant-Professor-Associate-Professor-Full-Professor-_REQ23038": {
      "title": "Director, Surgical Simulation and Technology (Assistant Professor/Associate Professor/Full Professor)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University seeks an outstanding academic educator and clinician for the full-time faculty position of Director of Surgical Simulation and Technology for the Department of Surgery and the General Surgery Residency Program.   The Director of Surgical Simulation and Technology provides leadership for the development, and implementation of simulation-based surgical education programs within the Department of Surgery. This role is responsible for managing all required surgical simulation curricula and training programs, including ACGME and American Board of Surgery requirements, while ensuring surgery residents and medical students receive comprehensive training in open, laparoscopic, endoscopic, and robotic surgical techniques. The Director develops and implements competency-based assessment methods, coordinates team-based simulation activities and works closely with faculty to promote engagement in surgical education and skills training. This position will be structured with 35% clinical responsibilities and 65% administrative responsibilities.   As a core faculty member of the General Surgery Residency Program, the Director provides direct teaching, supervision, and mentorship to residents and students in clinical, simulation, and classroom settings. The position fosters a culture of academic excellence by supporting resident-led scholarly activity, research and quality improvement initiatives. The Director serves as a professional role model and career mentor while contributing to the educational mission of the College of Medicine. Clinical responsibilities include providing surgical care, clinical teaching, and supervision of residents and medical students in operative and patient care settings.   The Director also collaborates with university and hospital leadership to advance simulation technologies, secure funding, and expand educational capabilities throughout the system. Responsibilities include guiding the acquisition of advanced simulation equipment, supporting the development of an American College of Surgeons Accredited Education Institute (AEI), and ensuring that simulation resources serve both surgical trainees and practicing healthcare professionals. The position performs additional projects and responsibilities as assigned in support of the department's strategic goals.   The successful candidate will be an ABS board-certified surgeon with a demonstrated commitment to graduate medical education, surgical education, patient safety, quality improvement, and resident professional development. Prior experience in GME leadership, ACGME accreditation, resident evaluation, recruitment, simulation, or quality improvement is preferred. The successful candidate will receive an academic faculty appointment in the Florida Atlantic University Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine, Department of Surgery, with academic rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. Minimum Qualifications: • MD or DO degree from an accredited medical school. • Completion of an ACGME-accredited General Surgery residency. • Board certification/eligibility in General Surgery. • Eligibility for an unrestricted Florida medical license and appropriate clinical privileges. • Demonstrated commitment to academic medicine, graduate medical education, teaching, and resident mentorship. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Clinical - Off Campus Location (COM use only) Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2027-01-01 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Coordinator--Administrative-Services_REQ22979": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Administrative Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Coordinator of Administrative Services. - Boca Raton, FL. The Division of Student Affairs is seeking a highly organized, detail-oriented, and collaborative professional to play an important role within Student Health Services. This position will coordinate communications and outreach efforts, support Executive Committee activities and organizational initiatives, and ensure the accurate and timely maintenance of provider credentialing and compliance documentation. Summary of responsibilities: Outreach and Strategic Communication Coordination: Responsible for coordinating outreach strategies to advance the organization’s mission, goals, & objectives. Set and track administrative and programmatic priorities for the SHS communications, outreach events, and related initiatives. Plan, coordinate, and staff outreach events and initiatives. Participate in institutional, divisional, and department-wide events as required. Develops regular program-specific reports as assigned and upon request. Works with the Student Health Advisory Council (SHAC) on FAU-sponsored projects. Works as the point person with Student Affairs Communications and Marketing to plan ongoing, recurring, and one-time communication efforts, including announcing significant changes to SHS programs and services and shaping information about SHS that appears online and in publications poduced by campus partners.  Executive Committee Support Supports Executive Committee with meeting agenda/minutes and projects such as benchmarking, surveys, research, training, and presentations. Supports SHS assessment, patient satisfaction, and quality improvement initiatives. Supports the Executive Committee with meeting and project follow-up, including preparation for subsequent meetings. Provides administrative support to SHS initiatives, including but not limited to maintaining the emergency phone list, supporting staff recognition and development (i.e., professional weeks, birthdays, etc.), and other staff event planning, accreditation preparation, policy and procedures tracking, newsletter preparation, and other administrative tracking and support. Provider Credentialing Manages the credentialing monitoring system to ensure the current licensure of all medical staff meets all federal and state credentialing requirements. This includes their licensure and education (e.g., medical school or residency graduation), Drug Enforcement Administration certification for prescribing, board certification, Florida clinician credentialing documents, history of liability insurance coverage, continuing education documentation, and NPI numbers. Maintain log and renewal dates for clinic certifications, licenses, and related renewals. Works collaboratively with SHS staff who oversee the CAQH (Council for Affordable Quality Healthcare) / DataSpring portal to maintain provider credentialing documentation. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).    For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $45,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Division of Student Affairs: Student Health Services Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am-5pm. Some nights and weekends required Application Deadline: 2026-10-28 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Identity-Management-Engineer--Senior_REQ23022": {
      "title": "Identity Management Engineer, Senior",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Office of Information Technology at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Identity Management Engineer, Senior - Boca Raton, FL Summary of Responsibilities: Lead the design, implementation, administration, and continuous improvement of Identity and Access Management (IAM) solutions across Development, Test, and Production environments. Serve as the technical lead for IAM initiatives, providing architectural guidance and subject matter expertise for authentication, authorization, identity governance, privileged access management, and lifecycle management solutions. Develop, maintain, and enforce IAM standards, procedures, and best practices, including Active Directory, LDAP, role-based access control (RBAC), and privileged access management. Lead the design and management of identity lifecycle processes, including provisioning, deprovisioning, access requests, approvals, certifications, and periodic access reviews. Provide technical leadership in the integration of enterprise applications, cloud services, and third-party systems with IAM platforms utilizing connectors, APIs, scripting, and automation. Develop and maintain advanced scripts, workflows, and automation solutions to improve operational efficiency, reduce risk, and streamline identity management processes. Lead infrastructure planning, upgrades, migrations, and patch management activities to maintain security, stability, and vendor supportability. Monitor system performance, capacity, availability, and security posture. Establish alerts, dashboards, and operational metrics to ensure service-level objectives are achieved. Lead troubleshooting efforts for complex IAM incidents, service disruptions, security events, and integration issues. Perform root cause analysis and implement corrective actions. Collaborate with Information Security, Infrastructure, Application Development, Database Administration, Cloud Services, and Network Services teams to develop secure and scalable identity solutions. Participate in security audits, compliance initiatives, risk assessments, and access certification activities to ensure adherence to institutional policies, regulatory requirements, and industry standards. Serve as the highest level of technical escalation for IAM-related issues and provide mentorship, training, and guidance to engineers, analysts, administrators, and project teams. Develop and maintain technical documentation, including architecture diagrams, implementation guides, operational procedures, runbooks, disaster recovery plans, and troubleshooting documentation. Evaluate emerging IAM technologies, industry trends, and security best practices, making recommendations for continuous improvement and modernization of the IAM program. Lead project planning, technical design reviews, implementation activities, and vendor engagements related to IAM initiatives. Support on-call activities and provide leadership during critical incidents and service restoration efforts. Perform other job-related duties as assigned by supervisor. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).  For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and one year of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and three years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $99,000 Annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: OIT: Enterprise Applications & Identity Management Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-21 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Davie/OELL-Director-of-Development-and-Special-Projects_REQ23000": {
      "title": "OELL Director of Development and Special Projects",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an OELL Director of Development and Special Projects - Davie, FL. The OELL Director of Development and Special Projects is responsible for leading, assisting, and supporting the School Leaders Program Coordinator/OELL Executive Director with planning and executing funded projects and initiatives, as well as managing special projects assigned to the Director. Summary of Responsibilities Collaborate with the School Leaders Program Coordinator and OELL Executive Director to develop and refine the strategic direction for special projects. Play a key role in the development and implementation of initiatives, including grants, professional learning service contracts, and related goals aimed at improving public education for all students, and especially those historically underserved and systemically disadvantaged. Develop and execute the Florida Educator Professional Learning Network (FEPLN) initiatives of monthly webinars and an annual two-day Convening. Oversee the development and implementation of micro credentials that are built with Canvas support and utilize badges and certificates generated through FAU-acquired badging providers, which are designed for educational leadership and related areas of PreK-12 education. This includes the development of a marketplace site and support for online learning, and planning and execution of schoolteacher and leader micro credentials, AI Leadership micro credentials, OELL-developed and implemented in-person leadership professional learning, and OELL-developed asynchronous and synchronous professional learning. Responsible for aiding in the development and submission of grant proposals to secure external funding for various initiatives. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and six years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and eight years of appropriate experience required. Preferred Qualifications: • Ed.D. or Ph.D. in Education, Educational Leadership, Research Methodology, or a related field. • Ability to implement projects independently, including common administrative and clerical work. • Proven experience in project management, research development, and grant writing. • Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. • Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. • Demonstrated ability to lead and collaborate in a team-oriented environment. • Familiarity with educational leadership and research in a university setting. Salary: Commiserate with experience and qualifications Exempt Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP) College or Department: College of Education: Educational Leadership & Research Methods Location: Davie Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday 8:00 AM - 5:00 PM Application Deadline: 2026-10-27 Special Instructions to Applicant: This is a research or research-related support position. As required by Florida Statutes Section 1010.35, a Foreign Influence Screening may be required. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Accounting-Coordinator_REQ22416": {
      "title": "Accounting Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Florida Atlantic University Foundation is seeking an Accounting Coordinator to support financial operations, gift accounting, reconciliations, compliance, and reporting activities in Boca Raton, FL. The Accounting Coordinator is expected to perform duties with a high degree of independence, initiative, and judgment. Summary of Responsibilities: Perform gift compliance review, including approving transactions, accounting journals, budgets, as well as requested research for assigned gifts.   Reconcile daily revenue/contribution data integration from CRM donor database (Raiser’s Edge) to Accounting System (Workday) by appropriate gift and revenue codes.  Complete regular bank reconciliations for cash accounts.  Complete and/or manage sales, property tax returns and state registrations as assigned.  Maintain general ledger, and monthly journal entries generated within the Foundation’s Office and from various departments within the organization.  Participate in the month-end and year-end close processes by preparing journal entries, account reconciliations, and performing necessary reviews and analyses.  Represent the department and the University in appropriate departmental, SUS, or State Committees.  Serve as liaison with other departments across the University, as necessary.  Support internal control procedures on accounting activities for the department/unit or Foundation.  Perform special projects and other job-related duties as assigned.  FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break   (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty -   Tuition assistance after   6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).  For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at  https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here:  Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience. For some positions assigned to this class special qualifications may be added to the minimum, such as possession of a State of Florida CPA certificate. Salary: $60,000 - $70,000 Annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: FAU Foundation Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-27 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position has been reposted, and the compensation has been updated. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
