    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Director--Alumni-Networks_REQ22695": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Alumni Engagement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Assistant Director, Alumni Engagement in Boca Raton, FL. The Assistant Director, Alumni Engagement, will manage alumni network engagement and growth initiatives within the Alumni and Community Engagement team and support other key strategic priorities for the department. Building a culture of philanthropy and dedication across all current and future alumni network communities is a large emphasis of this role. Additionally, identifying new and maximizing current network initiatives, both internally and externally, to enhance the experience of volunteer leaders and network members. This position includes other duties as assigned to support the University, Division, Alumni, and Community Engagement as a whole. This role is pivotal for the continued growth and engagement of the Florida Atlantic community. The ideal candidate should be passionate about fostering relationships, driving volunteer success, and ensuring continued development and sustainability across all current and future networks. Summary of Responsibilities: Alumni Networks: Assist in the leadership, support, training, and stewardship of all Florida Atlantic University Alumni network operations and initiatives for all current and future alumni networks (including afﬁnity, geographic, and professional networks). Recruit, train, and manage over 100 local and regional/out-of-state volunteers for network leadership positions. Align volunteer efforts with Alumni and Community Engagement’s strategic planning goals for engagement with key groups, including young alumni and geographic, affinity, and professional affiliation groups. Administer standard operating procedures for Florida Atlantic University Alumni networks, including budgets, sponsorships, community partnerships, brand representation/guidelines, social media, and volunteer roles and responsibilities. Identify FAU Alumni network opportunities in collaboration with team members based on geographic location, afﬁnity, and professional afﬁliations. Research and identify target populations and work with key alumni and/or community partners to maximize engagement in those areas. Support all FAU Alumni network events and activities in coordination with leadership volunteers and team members across Florida Atlantic and internal to the department. Travel to location-based FAU Alumni network events to engage with volunteer leaders and build relationships across Florida and other states. Through alumni networks, identify notable alumni, implement board priorities and liaison involvement, and maximize the department’s network strategy. Marketing and Communications: Develop and implement marketing plans to acquire and sustain the FAU Alumni network engagement. Manage FAU Alumni network communication initiatives in collaboration with leadership, volunteers, and staff. Draft and review a large volume of invitations/communications and other promotional materials in support of FAU Alumni network events and initiatives. Maintain the FAU Alumni network leaders resource guide, website, and any other areas to ensure all information is up to date and effectively communicated and followed by volunteer leaders and members. Implement strategies to support further promotion and growth of memberships through alumni network programming. Utilize platforms like Canva to generate network-based content. Sponsorships Identify community partners for sponsorship/trade partnership opportunities to assist with offsetting network costs and building community relationships to support FAU Alumni events and initiatives. Support the development and organization of sponsorship opportunities, presentations, and agreements. Alumni and Student Programming Support the planning and execution of numerous alumni programs such as signature events, recurring events, and athletics events, including tailgates, watch parties, and more. Collaborate with university partners to cultivate and identify notable alumni for engagement opportunities and award nominations. Assist with the cultivation, tracking, and spotlighting of alumni-owned and operated businesses. Through Alumni Scholarships, support the planning, promotion, and operation of scholarship recipient events and programs aimed to deepen and sustain recipients’ engagement with the alumni department. Develop content and communications plans to spotlight the Alumni Scholarships program. Data, Technology, and Finances: Ensure data integrity through weekly and monthly tracking and reporting of the FAU Alumni network initiatives in coordination with advancement services. Use data-informed strategies to drive decisions and allocate resources for the greatest possible impact. Maintain all volunteer and member data to ensure information is up to date. Track the network's budget and ﬁnances, such as expenses related to FAU Alumni network initiatives and purchases. Administer platforms like RENXT/Classic, Blackbaud, Hivebrite Alumni Portal, and Active Campaign. Additional Responsibilities: Travel to visit with prospects, meet with volunteers, and facilitate events. Collaborate with and support a variety of partners on and off campus. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).  For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at  https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here:  Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and four years of appropriate experience. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience in volunteer engagement, advancement/development, and/or alumni relations. Salary: $60,000 - $65,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Institutional Advancement: Alumni Affairs / Athletic Engagement Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m.; nights and weekends as needed. Travel as needed. Application Deadline: 2026-10-27 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Online-Programs-Admissions-Concierge_REQ23015": {
      "title": "Online Programs Admissions Concierge",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic Online is seeking an Online Programs Admissions Concierge in Boca Raton, FL. With over 30,000 students from all 50 states and over 180 countries, 21 intercollegiate teams, 180 plus degree programs, and an administration that thrives on discovery and excellence, FAU is pushing the boundaries of higher education. Florida Atlantic's faculty and staff are trailblazers and innovators with a passion for finding creative solutions while advancing science, art, and technology in all disciplines. Our work environment is a hub of cultures from across the nation and the world, making FAU a place where collaboration flourishes. The primary role of the Online Programs Admissions Concierge is to enroll new students into the university’s online programs. The Concierge will work with students from the point of interest through enrollment, resolving most enrollment questions and issues and escalating only the most complex issues to higher levels. The Online Programs Admissions Concierge is primarily responsible for inquiry follow-up, managing the admissions process, providing high-quality customer service via phone, online, and in person, and liaising with program directors and other enrollment services as needed. The role reports to the Director of Online Enrollment and Student Success at the Center for Online and Continuing Education and will work closely with staff in the Office of Undergraduate Admissions and the Graduate College. This role requires adaptability and comfort pivoting as priorities and initiatives evolve. Duties include, but are not limited to: Provides support to the Undergraduate and Graduate Admissions offices with oversight and management of the admissions process for all online programs’ applicants. Responsible for guiding prospective online students proactively through the admissions process from application through enrollment and towards a successful online learning experience by clearly communicating program requirements, transfer credits, payment options, time commitment, technology requirements, and student support services, to ensure students move through the process without any roadblocks. Responsible for assessing applications, handling documentation, collecting information, entering data in databases and maintaining accurate student academic records.  Lead resolution of complex admissions and onboarding cases requiring coordination across multiple academic and administrative units. Monitor the timely review of online programs applications received, accurate verification of information in student information systems (Banner, Slate, CAS, etc.), prompt communication with applicants, and assist as needed. Monitor and facilitate the timely and compliant processing of all admission decisions, including posting academic records, test scores, and admissions decisions. May need to facilitate changes/updates to the student record prior to matriculation. Troubleshoot admission issues to facilitate an orderly and timely admissions process for online programs. Track and monitor student visits (in person or virtual), communications, and applications for admissions, and prepare reports to track conversion and yield of applicants. Analyze inquiry, application, and enrollment data to identify trends, gaps, and opportunities for improving conversion and yield for online programs. Serve as a subject-matter expert on online admissions workflows, Banner and Slate processes, and cross-unit enrollment coordination, providing guidance and training support as needed. Serve as an admissions liaison and coordinate regular communication with the Undergraduate Admissions, the Graduate College, Center for Online and Continuing Education, and academic departments to ensure efficient and compliant processing of online undergraduate and graduate programs applications and related documents. Coordinate regular team meetings between Undergraduate Admissions, Graduate College, and the Center for Online and Continuing Education with the goal of promoting and maintaining efficiency in the online programs’ application process. Serve as a strategic enrollment partner by proactively identifying process improvements and enrollment barriers impacting online, transfer, returning, and second bachelor’s students. Develop and maintain collaborative recruitment and enrollment pipelines with Florida state colleges and other institutional partners in support of transfer student growth. Partners with academic departments to support program-specific enrollment strategies and address student concerns that impact persistence and matriculation. Support re-engagement strategies for former FAU students and second bachelor’s applicants interested in online programs. Participate in recruitment events and promote online undergraduate and graduate programs. Travel to other campuses or locations may be required for events or presentations. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience. Salary: $65,000.00 - $70,000.00 USD annually. Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP). College or Department: Florida Atlantic Online. Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00am - 5:00pm. Some evening and weekends will be required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-26 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Transfer-Admissions-Counselor_REQ23033": {
      "title": "Transfer Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Transfer Admissions Counselor. - Boca Raton, FL. Summary of responsibilities: Works with Assistant Director of Admissions at the Boca Raton campus to develop and implement procedures that will support admissions policies and facilitates student recruitment and admissions, assists with developing new undergraduate and graduate transfer recruitment plans for FAU. Establishes and maintains effective communication and rapport with Florida State College advisors , faculty and other administrators to promote FAU’s academic programs and transfer process. Counsels and advises prospective students, applicants and family members about opportunities at Florida Atlantic University. Visits state/community college campuses to meet with students and advise them on transfer guidelines, requirements, prerequisites, and other admissions related matters. Promotes the LINK Program and FAU transfer scholarships. Maintain contact with businesses, universities, community colleges, and community organizations on a regular basis. Participates in community outreach efforts.  Plans and implements workshops, presentations, events and programs to promote transfer admissions to FAU at schools, businesses and community events. Advises prospective transfer students on pathways to facilitate transfer to FAU.  Supervises and trains support personnel, when applicable, to ensure proper information is disseminated. Coordinates and partners with FAU’s internal stakeholders on transfer and admissions matters. Tracks and monitors student visits, communications, and applications for admissions, and prepares reports to show return on investment. Process documents includes creating applicant files, forwarding/ tracking documents to all FAU campuses, copying documents, recording all transactions and managing databases and reviewing admissions files. Provides relevant referrals to other student services. Examples include offices such as Military & Veterans Student Success Center, Student Accessibility Services, and FAU Commuter Student Services. Collaborates with Transfer Student Services Center & Family Engagement for enrollment process and onboarding experience. Attend and support New Student Orientation programs for transfer student. Performs other job related duties as assigned by direct supervisor. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:   Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.   State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.   State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.   Sick Leave Pool Program.   Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).   Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).     For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor's degree from an accredited institution an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience; or a master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization required. This position requires daily contact with students, faculty, staff, and the general public, which includes prospective transfer student advising. Ability to operate a motor vehicle, qualify for car rental, and valid Florida driver’s license are required. Local and regional travel are an integral part of this position. Salary: $50,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Undergraduate Admissions Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday 8am - 5pm. Must be available to work on occasional evenings and weekends. Application Deadline: 2026-11-09 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/CA-AI-Research-Operations-Manager_REQ23039": {
      "title": "CA-AI Research Operations Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Division of Research at Florida Atlantic University is seeking a CA-AI Research Operations Manager - Boca Raton, FL. Center for Connected Autonomy and Artificial Intelligence (CCA-AI) is a leading interdisciplinary research center focused on advancing artificial intelligence, autonomous systems, and resilient wireless networking across underwater, surface, air, and space environments. The center conducts cutting-edge research in areas such as autonomous communications, machine learning, GPS-denied navigation, spectrum sharing, and intelligent decision-making for complex operational environments. CCA-AI brings together a collaborative team of faculty, researchers, and students dedicated to developing innovative technologies with real-world impact. This position offers the opportunity to contribute to pioneering research while helping shape the next generation of AI-enabled autonomous systems. Summary of Responsibilities: Support the administration of the CA_AI lab's growing research portfolio of federal and privately sponsored research programs. ​ Assist with proposal development, including budget preparation; materials collection (e.g., biosketches, current and pending); narrative framing; proofreading and editing; and compliance checks. Support project management activities, including tracking and reporting of technical deliverables. Manage project compliance activities, including scheduled and ad hoc reporting. Managing CA_AI lab students and volunteers. Manage the tracking and ordering of lab supplies and equipment, and coordinate maintenance scheduling as needed. Serve as a liaison between CA-AI and sponsor administrative teams. Represent CA-AI at relevant meetings, both internally and externally. Assist the Director in coordinating and participating in meetings with sponsors and external stakeholders. Collaborate closely with the Associate Director for Research Programs in I-SENSE and the Administrator of Office Operations to ensure the optimal success of the CA_AI Lab. Perform other job-related duties as assigned by the CA-AI Director. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).  For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $60,000 - $70,000 Annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Institute for Smarter Cities, Spaces, and Health Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday 8a.m-5p.m Application Deadline: 2026-11-05 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
