    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Program-Associate_REQ23042": {
      "title": "Program Associate",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Program Associate - Boca Raton, Fl. The Program Associate position supports the daily operations and administration of Florida Atlantic University laboratory research program, including managing research spaces, laboratory supplies, safety compliance, agreements, and administrative processes. This role coordinates research opportunities and course registration for FAU High School students, facilities, partnerships between student and university researchers, and supports research progress and program activities. Summary of responsibilities: Assist with the development, coordination, and processing of research-related memoranda of understanding and other agreements. Schedule the use of MRIC laboratories and research spaces. Manage ordering, inventory, and organization of laboratory supplies and materials. Assist with tracking Environmental Health and Safety (EHS) requirements and compliance for students, faculty, staff, and other laboratory users. Support the efficient day-to-day operation and utilization of MRIC research spaces. Coordinate with appropriate university offices to facilitate the listing and scheduling of FAU High School research courses. Promote research course opportunities to eligible students and assist with student registration processes. Manage research course registration permissions and related administrative requirements. Serve as a point of coordination for Florida Atlantic faculty and researchers interested in providing research opportunities to FAU High School students. Assist with matching qualified students with university researchers, laboratories, projects, and research opportunities. Support the research program in reviewing student progress and coordinating feedback on student research work. Maintain appropriate records related to student participation in research courses and experiences. Maintain inventories and coordinate the ordering of laboratory materials and supplies for elementary science and MRIC laboratories. Mediate teacher requests for research activities, laboratory experiences, demonstrations, and curriculum-integrated research opportunities. Coordinate schedules, assignments, and activities for work-study students supporting the research program. Support the STARs Program by coordinating student participation in curriculum activities, maintaining schedules, tracking EH&S compliance, and documenting student service hours. Manage the Florida Atlantic University Laboratory Schools’ research newsletter, including soliciting content, organizing submissions, developing monthly drafts, and coordinating distribution through designated communication channels. Develop and post appropriate content to the research program social media accounts and other approved communication platforms. Assist in highlighting student, faculty, and partner research accomplishments, publications, presentations, awards, and other achievements. Maintain organized records and information that support reporting and communication of research program activities and outcomes. Assist with research-related travel authorizations, purchasing documentation, expense reports, and other administrative processes. Organize scheduling for research program meetings, collaborative meetings, research teams, university partners, and external stakeholders. Provide general administrative support to the Director of Research and the Laboratory Schools Research Program. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). undefinedFor details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma and five years of appropriate experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience required. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree in an appropriate specialization from an accredited university. Two (2) years of related experience. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong technology skills and the ability to learn university administrative, scheduling, registration, purchasing, and communication systems. Ability to work effectively and collaboratively with K–12 students, teachers, university faculty, researchers, administrators, and external partners. Experience with research program administration or coordination. K–12 or higher education experience. Experience in university research environments or laboratories. Experience with student research programs, internships, or experiential learning. Excellent organizational and project-management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Strong attention to detail and ability to maintain accurate records. Ability to coordinate complex schedules, activities, projects, and events involving multiple stakeholders. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain appropriate confidentiality when working with students and research-related information. Interest in research, STEM education, student research, innovation, and the integration of university research opportunities into K–12 education. A positive, service-oriented approach and the ability to adapt effectively within a dynamic research and educational environment. Salary: $50,000 - $53,000 Annually. College or Department: COE: FAUS - District and School Programs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 7:30 a.m. - 4 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-11-01 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Professor_REQ23004": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The IT & Operations Management (ITOM) Department in the College of Business at Florida Atlantic University seeks to hire one tenure-track Assistant Professor in Applied Artificial Intelligence (AI)  & Business Analytics for employment starting Fall 2027.  Responsibilities:  The successful candidate will teach AI, Business Analytics, and Management Information Systems courses in both undergraduate and graduate programs, including MBA and doctoral programs; must maintain an active program of research and publication in Applied AI and Business Analytics; and will participate in appropriate service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. Emphasis will be placed on producing scholarly research in top-tier peer-reviewed Information Systems and related business journals.  For More Information: For questions or additional information about this position, please contact the search committee chair, Dr. Ravi Behara, at rbehara@fau.edu . Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate in Applied Artificial Intelligence, Business Analytics, Management Information Systems, or a related field from a university with AACSB or similar accreditation conferred by the effective date of employment. Demonstrated record of ability to publish quality scholarly research in peer-reviewed academic journals and conferences. Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching as instructor of record at an accredited (AACSB or similar) university. Certification or experience in online teaching preferred. The ideal candidate will have research and teaching interests focused on Applied Artificial Intelligence and Business Analytics. However, all related areas of teaching and research focus will be considered. Related industry experience is strongly desired. Salary: To be discussed with applicant. College or Department: College of Business Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Full-Time Application Deadline: 2027-06-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: This is a research or research-related support position. As required by Florida Statutes Section 1010.35, a Foreign Influence Screening may be required. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: letter of application detailing how candidate meets qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy and quality (with recent teaching evaluation scores or awards included, if applicable), sample of current research (if applicable), and professional references (name, affiliation, contact information). Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Director-of-Student-Services_REQ23027": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Student Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Assistant Director of Student Services - Boca Raton, FL. The Assistant Director for Student Services manages a diverse portfolio of complex student programs, projects, and events, establishing priorities, coordinating resources, and ensuring timely execution of initiatives that enhance student engagement, support student success, and enrich the medical student experience. This position serves as the Director's designee in their absence and supports the achievement of departmental and university goals through effective planning, communication, program administration, and relationship-building with students, faculty, alumni, and community partners. Summary of Responsibilities Program Support Assists the Assistant Dean for Student Affairs, Associate Dean for Student Affairs and Admissions, Senior Director of Student Affairs and Student Services, and faculty leaders with the administration, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of student affairs programs, including Career Advising, Parliament Learning Communities, the M1/M2 Shadowing Program, Gold Humanism Honor Society, Schwartz Rounds, and other departmental initiatives. Manages shadowing program operations, including participant assignments, experience tracking, feedback collection, and program evaluation. Provides administrative and operational support for the Gold Humanism Honor Society and related student initiatives. Provides additional support for Office of Student Affairs programs and initiatives as assigned. Supports the administration, tracking, documentation, and secure record management of student cases within Maxient.  Event Support Coordinates, plans, and executes College of Medicine student programs, ceremonies, and special events, including New Student Orientation, White Coat Ceremony, Year 2 Orientation, Transition Weeks/Orientations, Alpha Omega Alpha Medical Honor Society Induction Ceremony, Research & Scholarship Day, Gold Humanism Honor Society Induction and Award Ceremony, Match Day, Commencement, Recognition Ceremony and Reception, community engagement events, and other institutional programs. Oversees all aspects of event management, including timelines, agendas, programs, speakers, communications, scripting, logistics, vendor coordination, and event operations. Collaborates with Communications, Educational Affairs, Development, faculty, alumni, students, and external partners to ensure successful event execution. Assists with administration of donor-funded student programs and related events. Student Communications Develops and maintains Office of Student Affairs communications, including website content, social media content, marketing materials, event promotion, student messaging, and communication strategies designed to improve engagement and effectiveness, in coordination with the Communications Department. Alumni Engagement Assists with the development, implementation, expansion, and promotion of College of Medicine alumni mentoring, networking, and engagement programs. Serves as a liaison among alumni, students, faculty, and institutional partners to support mentoring and engagement initiatives. Student Engagement, Organizations, and Research Advises class councils, student interest groups, and student organizations in accordance with university policies and procedures. Provides guidance and support for student organization operations, planning, and activities. Collaborates with the College of Medicine Research Department and Research Director to support Medical Student Research Day, research symposia, and other student research initiatives. Serves as primary coordinator for student apparel, promotional items, and merchandise orders. Community Partnerships and Engagement Serves as a liaison among Career Advisors, student leaders, affiliate faculty, community physicians, clinical partners, and other stakeholders to support student development, experiential learning, and community engagement initiatives. Collaborates with the Community Engagement Office to support student-led projects, service activities, and community partnerships. General Serves as backup support for VSLO, Alumni Credentialing Support, ERAS, and other residency application services, including verification of academic standing, collection and review of required documentation, data verification, and maintenance of confidentiality in all student and Office of Student Affairs matters. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and four years of appropriate experience required. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree and three years of experience. Progressively responsible senior-level administrative, operational, management, or related professional experience. Experience in a higher education institution, medical school, or hospital. Ability to work collaboratively with all levels of faculty, staff, and students. Exceptional verbal and written communication skills are essential for success in this position. Proficiency in Microsoft Office programs such as Word, Outlook, PowerPoint and Excel. Exceptional customer service, organizational and time management skills. Salary: $66,000 - $70,000 Annually. College or Department: COM: Student Affairs Administration Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Application Deadline: 2026-11-05 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Longitudinal-Integrated-Clerkship-Administrator_REQ22998": {
      "title": "Longitudinal Integrated Clerkship Administrator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Office of Medical Education at Florida Atlantic University is seeking a detail-oriented and proactive individual to join our team as a Longitudinal Integrated Clerkship Administrator in Boca Raton, FL. The Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University is dedicated to providing exceptional medical education and fostering the development of future physicians and healthcare leaders.  Our Longitudinal Integrated Clerkship (LIC) offers a unique learning experience that integrates clinical training across multiple specialties. This administrative position plays a critical role in supporting the implementation and coordination of our LIC program within the Year 3 curriculum, including administering the learning management platform, tracking student assignments, coordinating academic sessions, and fostering relationships with affiliate faculty members. Summary of Responsibilities Manage and maintain the learning management platform used for the LIC program, ensuring that it meets the needs of students, faculty, and staff. Provide technical support and training to users, troubleshoot issues, and implement enhancements as needed. Track student assignments and progress throughout the LIC program, maintaining accurate records and documentation. Communicate with students and faculty regarding assignments, deadlines, and requirements. Coordinate logistics for educational sessions including scheduling, room reservations, catering, and audiovisual support. Collaborate with faculty members to develop session agendas and secure guest speakers or presenters as needed. Assist in the development and coordination of activities for other Year 3 curriculum components. Foster positive relationships with affiliate faculty members who participate in the LIC program, serving as a point of contact for communication and support. Coordinate orientation sessions and ongoing training opportunities for affiliate faculty to ensure their success in teaching and mentoring students. Collaborate with the Office of Program Evaluation and Assessment team to support data collection, analysis, and reporting related to the LIC program and outcomes, identifying areas for improvement. Collaborate with the Year 3 leadership team to implement changes and enhancements based on feedback and assessment data. Serve as a proctor for exams across the undergraduate medical education curriculum. Support administrative operations in other areas of the curriculum as needed. Attend and support College of Medicine and medical education special events as needed. Complete special projects and/or other duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization (i.e. education, health care administration, or a related field) and 1 year of appropriate professional/specialized experience or a high school diploma and 5 years of appropriate professional/specialized experience required. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. A bachelor’s degree is highly preferred. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience in an administrative role, preferably within a healthcare or academic setting. Advanced proficiency in Microsoft Office, including Excel, Word, Outlook, mail merges, bulk communications, calendar management, and high-volume scheduling workflows. Proficiency with Microsoft Teams and Zoom, including scheduling sessions, supporting virtual meetings, and managing breakout rooms. Ability to use technology to streamline workflows, improve communication, and manage large volumes of student, faculty, site, and curricular information. Familiarity with process improvement and automation tools, such as Power Automate and PowerShell. Exceptional verbal and written communication skills Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders within the university and health care community Proficiency in using learning management systems and other educational technology tools. Ability to respect and navigate sensitive issues and maintain confidentiality in all matters. Consistently demonstrate a high level of professionalism. Salary: $48,000 Annually. College or Department: 01044807 Longitudinal Integrated Clerkship Administrator Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Occasional extended morning, evening, and weekend hours as needed. Application Deadline: 2026-10-27 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Academic-Advisor-I_REQ22969": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor I",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Academic Advisor I . - Boca Raton, FL. The Department of Undergraduate Studies is recruiting two Academic Advisor I openings. By applying to this recruitment, you will be eligible for both openings. The Academic Advisor I position provides a safety net for any student not sure where to go for help. This role provides a comprehensive array of services aimed at aiding students in developing and implementing an appropriate and meaningful education plan. Summary of Responsibilities Provides academic advising to all first and second-year students, including transfer students at FAU with under 45 earned credit hours and all undeclared students regardless of hours earned. Serves as liaison to an assigned college or student support unit on campus. Clears undergraduate registration holds and responds to email inquiries and phone messages. Assists with campus events, such as the Admissions Office open houses, University Expos, and other evening and weekend duties requiring a UAS advising presence. In support of our FTIC and second-year students, this position will require some evening and virtual hours on a rotating basis. Assist students with developing academic and career action plans, work and support undecided students, students in academic difficulty, and students transitioning into their major of choice. Perform other job-related tasks as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization required. Preferred Qualifications: A master's degree in education, Student Affairs/Development, Counselor Education, Psychology, or a related field. One year of experience in advising, counseling, orientation, student services, or related experience at a university is preferred. Graduate internships can be applied toward one-year experience. Proficiency in working with computer programs, specifically Microsoft Word, Access, Outlook, and Excel. The ability to communicate effectively and professionally. Working knowledge of the Appreciative Advising model. Salary: $55,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: University Advising Services Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Mondays - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-11-03 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Harbor-Branch-HBOI/Research-Machinist_REQ22382-1": {
      "title": "Research Machinist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute at Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Research Machinist in Harbor Branch Fort Pierce, FL. FAU Harbor Branch,   located   in Ft. Pierce, is a research institute focusing on marine science and oceanography with over 200 scientists, staff and students that work and study at the site.    The Research Machinist provides specialized machining and fabrication support for oceanographic research at the Harbor Branch Oceanographic Institute. Responsible for CNC and manual machining, prototype development, and collaboration with engineers and scientists to design, build, and test advanced oceanographic equipment, while supporting project planning, maintenance, and safe shop operations. Summary of Responsibilities: Machining Operations and Equipment: Responsible for programming, setting up, and operating CNC milling and turning equipment using CAD/CAM software, as well as operating manual machinery. Collaborates with FAU HBOI engineers, scientists, and clients to develop, manufacture, and test advanced oceanographic equipment and instrumentation. Contributes manufacturing insights and technical guidance to refine early-stage design concepts. Provides manufacturing advice to researchers designing proof-of-concept prototypes. Coordinating and planning: Performs tasks related to planning, building, and testing oceanographic equipment, and makes independent decisions on fabrication when necessary. Prepares manufacturing time estimates for project scheduling and procurement. Creates and maintains production schedules. Preventive maintenance and Repairs: Performs preventative equipment maintenance and coordinates required repairs. Maintains a safe, clean work environment in compliance with FAU HBOI health and safety regulations. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its   perks ! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:   Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.   State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.   State employees   Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)   program.   Sick Leave Pool Program.   Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at   President’s   discretion).   Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition   assistance   after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).     For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at   https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in St. Lucie County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the   area   a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here:   St Lucie County, FL Things to Do, Restaurants & More - Treasure Coast Minimum Qualifications: Completion of an approved machinist apprenticeship program; or a high school diploma and five years of appropriate experience including CNC Machine programing of mill and lathe, setup and operation of CNC mill and lathe, and manual mill and lathe experience required. Appropriate vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Required Qualifications and Skills: Must have valid Florida Driver's license and acceptable driving record. Basic knowledge of machining plastics and aluminum. Ability to read and interpret design blueprints and mechanical drawings. Must be able to communicate effectively with all levels of employees and managers. Must be able to work flexible schedule as determined by supervisor. Generate designs and blueprints using CAD software. Program and operate CNC machining equipment. Salary: $28.00-$32.00 per hour College or Department: HBOI: Engineering Services Location: Harbor Branch (HBOI) Work Days and Hours: Monday – Friday, 8:00 AM -5:00 PM Application Deadline: 2026-11-03 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. VETERANS’ PREFERENCE: Applicants may claim Veterans’ Preference on their application. The applicant claiming preference is responsible for providing required documentation at the time of making an application in Workday for a vacant position, or prior to the closing date of the vacancy announcement. If an applicant qualifies for Veterans' Preference and the SP position, they are shown preference by the guarantee of an interview. Veterans’ Preference does not guarantee a job. For additional information, please visit https://www.fau.edu/jobs/resources/veterans/. For assistance, please contact Recruitment Services at empl@fau.edu. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover Letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Director-of-Financial-and-Personnel-Operations_REQ23032": {
      "title": "Director of Financial and Personnel Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Director of Financial and Personnel Operations - Boca Raton, FL. The Director of Financial and Personnel Operations serves as the primary point of contact for all financial, budgetary, human resources, and day-to-day operations of the College. Areas of responsibility include management of all financial accounting operations, including development of the annual operating budget, preparation of regular budget reports, oversight of state, federal grant, and foundation funding, purchasing, and fiscal management of all College business matters. Summary of Responsibilities Serves as the College of Nursing’s liaison with the Provost's office on all financial, budgetary, and human resource (HR) matters. Develops and implements University fiscal policies and procedures related to the College of Nursing, ensuring compliance with State standards. Interprets University and State policies and procedures; develops procedures to comply with audit recommendations. Formulates, coordinates, and maintains fiscal policies within the area of the College of Nursing; assures adherence to the same. Provides leadership and direction in policy development. Works directly with the Dean of the College of Nursing and the Office of the Provost to develop, implement, administer, and evaluate programs to accomplish the mission and goals of the College of Nursing in alignment with the mission and vision of FAU as they relate to all fiscal (financial and budgetary) and administrative issues. Interacts daily with the Dean and all Associate and Assistant Deans and Directors, as well as faculty, students, and administrative staff within the University, other State agencies, and vendors. Scope of contact includes disseminating information, responding to inquiries, negotiating fees and services, and providing direct assistance and instruction on budgetary matters and personnel issues. Oversees personnel matters for the Dean and trains and assists the departments in all aspects of budgetary, financial, and personnel matters. Trains and assists finance and HR employees within the college. Assists with the development of strategies leading to the successful accreditation of the College of Nursing Provides financial oversight of Memory and Wellness Center, Community Health Center, Auxiliary, and Foundation budgets and preparation and submission of the Research Center's Annual Reports to the Board of Governors. Provides financial oversight of the College of Nursing’s auxiliary, self-supporting programs; supports and analyzes their/its budgetary, human resource, and financial operations, as necessary. Provides personnel and financial data for surveys to outside agencies (i.e., American Association of College of Nursing, Southern Regional Education Board). Represents the College of Nursing on the Workday-related committees. Oversees the College of Nursing's Clinical Practice Organization (CPO) for the College, the Memory and Wellness Center, the FAU Community Health Center, and the FAU Northwest Community Health Alliance, Inc. clinic. Identifies appropriate clinical billing consultants for the College of Nursing's Clinical Practice Organization (CPO), the Memory and Wellness Center, the FAU Community Health Center, and the FAU Northwest Community Health Alliance, Inc. clinic and makes arrangements for review and training of providers and staff as necessary Serves as Treasurer and Secretary for the College of Nursing’s Clinical Practice Organization (CPO), supporting the CPO Board with financial oversight, governance, and required organizational records and documentation.  Coordinates and works with internal and external auditors on an annual basis for the CPO, including providing requested financial records, supporting documentation, and responses to audit inquiries and recommendations.  Represents Nursing on the Faculty Practice/CPO/SIP Logistics Group. Prepares consolidated budgets for presentation to the CPO board. Reviews and analyzes all clinical revenue reports of receivables, billings, and payments for the CHC and MWC clinics Oversees, supports, and analyzes all FAU Community Health Center and FAU Northwest Community Health Alliance, Inc. clinics’ budgetary, HR, and financial operations and reporting. Works with all FAU departments and other internal/external constituents on financial and operational transactions and related reporting. Consolidates all clinical practice data for the College and Centers to submit for the annual Self Insurance Premium (SIP) liability coverage, serving as direct point of contact and liaison on all inquiries. Provides consultation, oversight, expertise, direction, and support on all ad hoc projects as assigned.  Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and six years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and eight years of appropriate experience required. Salary: $110,000.00 - $125,000.00 USD Annual. Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP) College or Department: College of Nursing Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm Application Deadline: 2026-11-02 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Assistant-Director--Department-Administration_REQ22884": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Department Administration",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Assistant Director, Department Administration - Boca Raton, FL. The Assistant Director, Department Administration position supports the mission of the College of Engineering and Computer Science. This role is tasked with enhancing department operational efficiency, supporting research initiatives, and contributing to student success. The College of Engineering and Computer Science at Florida Atlantic University is dedicated to shaping the future through cutting-edge research and transformative education. Summary of Responsibilities Assist faculty in preparing and budgeting grant proposals, ensuring compliance with internal and external submission guidelines. Track proposal submissions and manage awarded research grants, including monitoring expenditures and preparing financial reports. Develop and maintain a robust fiscal tracking system for various department accounts (e.g., GTAIDS, Auxiliary, Foundation, Tech Fee, Carryforward). Conduct budget forecasting, amendments, and reconciliations to ensure fiscal responsibility and compliance. Stay abreast of evolving federal, state, and university policies affecting research and administrative practices. Advise department members on compliance matters and implement policy changes as needed. Serve as a primary contact for Principal Investigators (PIs) and central research offices, facilitating communication and report submissions. Prepare and submit Research Center Reports to the Board of Governors and highlight department research achievements. Oversee purchasing functions, including approval of pCard transactions, preparation of requisitions, and monitoring of financial activities. Manage administrative staff, providing training, conducting performance evaluations, and fostering professional development. Pre-certify effort reports for research awards and manage tuition waivers in accordance with university policies. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and four years of appropriate experience required. Valid Florida Driver's License required. Preferred Qualifications: Degree in business administration, finance, accounting, public administration, higher education administration, or a related field. Experience managing departmental and sponsored research budgets, including budget development, forecasting, reconciliation, expenditure monitoring, and financial reporting. Experience supporting pre-award and post-award research administration, including proposal budgeting, grant submissions, award management, and compliance with sponsor requirements. Working knowledge of federal, state, and institutional regulations governing sponsored research and university financial activities. Experience working directly with faculty and Principal Investigators to manage research funding and resolve administrative or financial issues. Experience supervising, training, and evaluating administrative staff. Strong analytical and organizational skills, with demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, and complex financial information. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft Excel and demonstrated ability to develop and maintain financial tracking and reporting tools. Strong written and verbal communication skills and demonstrated ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, students, central administrative offices, and external stakeholders. Salary: $60,000 - $66,000 Annually. College or Department: COECS: Ocean and Mechanical Engineering & Seatech Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-26 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Admissions-Counselor_REQ23025": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Admissions Counselor - Boca Raton, FL. The Admissions Counselor position is responsible for the recruitment and advisement of prospective FAU students across assigned territories. The Admissions Counselor must collaborate with key stakeholders within and outside of the university. The Admissions Counselor is also responsible for participating in student outreach events and giving presentations during the recruitment cycle, providing a thorough understanding of FAU's policies and procedures, and performing other tasks as assigned. Summary of Responsibilities Responsible for developing and implementing recruitment activities for assigned counties in Florida, as well as other key recruitment markets nationwide. Work with regional alumni in cooperation with the Alumni and Admissions Offices to support the University's recruitment efforts. Partner and collaborate with staff and faculty in Student Affairs, Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, and other key stakeholders for recruitment, onboarding, and enrollment of new students. Establish and maintain effective communication and rapport with high school counselors and state college advisors. Counsel and advise prospective students, applicants, and family members about opportunities at Florida Atlantic University. Manage a recruitment territory, using data, data analytics tools, and university dashboards to drive decisions, and consider ROI in recruitment events, travel, and marketing efforts. Responsible and accountable for generating reports, informing, and meeting goals within their territory and providing input to admissions and student affairs leadership to inform the bigger enrollment picture. Provide In-person, phone, email, and text to communicate with potential students. Responsible for participating in high school visits, college nights/fairs, presentations through multiple communication channels, and call nights throughout the recruiting cycle, with travel and evening and weekend participation as needed to support recruitment activities. Responsible for representing the entire university to prospective students, families, and high school guidance counselors. Utilizes an understanding of university policies and procedures, a professional presence, and gives accurate information while abiding by the university and higher education best practices. Supporting on-campus visit programs as needed. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization and two years or appropriate experience; or a master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate area of specialization required. Valid driver's license. Local, and regional travel is an integral part of this position. Excellent communication skills, both oral and written, are essential. Ability to operate a motor vehicle, qualify for car rental, and a valid Florida driver’s license are required. This position requires daily contact with students, faculty, staff, and the general public, which includes prospective student advising Salary: $50,000 annually. Exempt Administrative, Managerial, Professional (AMP) College or Department: Undergraduate Admissions Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8am- 5pm. Occasional evenings and weekends required. Application Deadline: 2026-10-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Purchasing-Agent-III_REQ23051": {
      "title": "Purchasing Agent III",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Division of Financial Affairs at Florida Atlantic University is seeking a Purchasing Agent III (Position # 990964) in Boca Raton, FL. The Purchasing Agent III is responsible for developing, coordinating, and executing strategic procurement and contracting activities in support of the University community. Provides comprehensive procurement services throughout the procurement and contract lifecycle, ensuring compliance with Florida State University System Board of Governors (BOG) regulations, applicable procurement regulations and policies, and all relevant federal, state, and local laws. Promotes effective competition, cost efficiency, risk mitigation, contract compliance, and best value through sound procurement strategies, market research, financial analysis, and supplier relationship management. Serves as a procurement advisor and strategic partner to University departments, supporting institutional objectives through transparent, accountable, and results-oriented procurement practices. Summary of Responsibilities: Strategic Procurement and Stakeholder Engagement Develops, coordinates, and executes procurement strategies for assigned spend categories and commodities in alignment with University priorities, operational requirements, and applicable regulatory frameworks. Collaborates with departments across the Division of Financial Affairs and the broader University community to assess procurement needs, establish sourcing strategies, evaluate alternatives, and develop solutions that achieve operational objectives and deliver best value. Serves as a procurement liaison and advisor to end-user departments, project managers, and other stakeholders, providing guidance on procurement policies, procedures, competitive requirements, contracting options, and applicable BOG regulations and state statutes. Manages multiple procurement initiatives concurrently in a fast-paced, service-oriented environment, balancing competing priorities, project milestones, regulatory requirements, and established deadlines.   Procurement Lifecycle and Competitive Solicitations Coordinates and supports the full procurement lifecycle, from initial requirements assessment and sourcing strategy through solicitation, evaluation, award, contract execution, and ongoing contract administration. Develops, coordinates, and administers competitive solicitation documents, including Invitations to Negotiate (ITNs), Requests for Proposals (RFPs), and Invitations to Bid (ITBs), ensuring requirements are clearly defined, evaluation methodologies are appropriate, and solicitation processes comply with applicable regulations and University policies. Conducts market research and supplier outreach to identify qualified sources, assess market conditions, evaluate available solutions, and promote effective competition.  Analyzes and evaluates procurement alternatives, including state, county, cooperative, and other authorized public-sector contract vehicles, to identify compliant sourcing opportunities and maximize institutional value. Participates in bid and proposal evaluations, conducts cost comparisons and financial analyses, assesses supplier responses, and develops recommendations based on documented evaluation criteria, operational requirements, compliance considerations, and overall value to the University. Contract Development and Administration Coordinates the review, negotiation, routing, execution, and modification of supplier contracts, purchase orders, and change orders in accordance with University policies, delegated authority, and applicable regulatory requirements. Supports contract administration and management throughout the contract term, including monitoring contract expenditures, purchase order balances, invoice activity, deliverables, renewal provisions, expiration dates, and other critical contractual milestones. Collaborate with end-user departments, Accounts Payable, project stakeholders, and other relevant units to resolve contract-related issues, address supplier performance concerns, and promote timely and accurate invoice processing. Assists in the resolution of supplier disputes, contractual discrepancies, performance issues, and other procurement-related matters, escalating issues as appropriate to protect the University’s interests. Maintains accurate and complete procurement documentation to support transparency, accountability, internal controls, and audit readiness. Compliance, Risk Management, and Operational Effectiveness Interprets and applies applicable BOG regulations, state statutes, University procurement policies, and other relevant requirements to procurement and contracting activities. Identifies potential compliance gaps, contractual risks, process deficiencies, and opportunities to strengthen procurement controls; recommends appropriate corrective actions and risk mitigation strategies. Promotes consistent application of procurement requirements and supports the development of compliant, defensible, and well-documented procurement decisions. Utilizes the Workday enterprise resource planning (ERP) system and other designated procurement technologies to facilitate procurement transactions, maintain accurate records, monitor contract activity, and support effective workflow management. Prepares, analyzes, and interprets reports related to procurement activity, contract utilization, expenditures, spend patterns, supplier performance, and operational trends to support informed decision-making and continuous improvement. Customer Service and Organizational Support Provides professional, responsive, and solutions-oriented service to University departments, suppliers, and other stakeholders while maintaining the integrity of procurement policies and established controls. Communicates procurement requirements, timelines, procedures, and decisions clearly and effectively to stakeholders with varying levels of procurement knowledge. Identifies opportunities to streamline workflows, improve procurement practices, strengthen internal controls, and enhance service delivery. Provides cross-functional support and serves as a backup for other Procurement functions to maintain operational continuity and meet departmental needs. Performs other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).    For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php     Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution of higher education in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of relevant professional experience. Demonstrated experience in procurement and contracting, including competitive solicitations, contract development and administration, supplier negotiations, sourcing analysis, and supplier relationship management. Knowledge of procurement principles, competitive purchasing practices, contract management, and regulatory compliance requirements. Demonstrated analytical, problem-solving, organizational, and project management skills, including the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet established deadlines. Strong written and verbal communication, stakeholder engagement, negotiation, and customer service skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and PowerPoint. Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience in public higher education procurement Experience developing and administering complex competitive solicitations, including ITNs, RFPs, and ITBs. Experience with Euna Solutions/Bonfire or comparable electronic public procurement and solicitation platforms. Experience with Workday ERP or comparable enterprise procurement and financial management systems. Familiarity with Florida public-sector procurement requirements, including applicable BOG regulations, state statutes, and University procurement policies. Experience conducting market research, cost and pricing analyses, supplier evaluations, contract utilization reviews, and procurement reporting. Demonstrated ability to identify procurement risks, strengthen internal controls, improve processes, and support audit-ready documentation. Required Licenses, Certifications, and/or Other Specific Requirements of Law: Valid driver’s license required. Subject to a criminal background check, which may include Level II screening in accordance with Florida Statute §435.04. Position is subject to applicable federal and state privacy regulations. Salary: $58,000.00 - $80,000.00 Commensurate with experience College or Department: Division of Financial Affairs Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m Application Deadline: 2026-10-30 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position may close without prior notice. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Pine-Jog-Environmental-Education-Center/Afterschool-Office-Assistant_REQ22650": {
      "title": "Afterschool Office Assistant",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Pine Jog Environmental Education Center of Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Afterschool Office Assistant - West Palm Beach, FL. Afterschool Office Assistant helps support a quality afterschool program for the students that attend Pine Jog Elementary School. Our goal is to meet the fundamental needs for growth and development for all children attending our program by providing a safe and healthy environment. It is important that children be given the best possible opportunities to grow into healthy, well-adjusted youth. Responsible for assisting with program operations, administration, and clerical support activities. Summary of Responsibilities: Recommends policy for program operations and advises faculty/administrators in the unit regarding interpretations, applications, and implementation of new or revised rules, policies, and procedures. Assist in the development and implementation of a school-age childcare (SACC) program and summer camp program. Integrate environmental education and program inventory. Maintain Sign-In and Sign-Out Duties. Responsible for monitoring that all parent’s signatures are accurate with names and times. Maintain all registrar forms are up to date in our ProCare system. Create and review attendance lists. Make sure that Accident and Incident Reports supplies are always available and that they are filed away accurately. Make sure ELC sign-in and sign-out sheets are submitted in a timely manner. Attend meetings conduct observations, participate in the scoring meetings and submit notes to the Director or Assistant Director. Negotiate contracts for a variety of services. Filing, checking phone and ProCare messages, maintaining program master calendar updates, and performing other job-related duties as assigned. FAU Benefits and Perks   If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers:  Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more.  State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans.  State employees  Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF)  program.  Sick Leave Pool Program.  Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion).  Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day   Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply).  For details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at  https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County   The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here:  Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB   Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma and four years of appropriate experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Salary: $17.00 hourly. Non-Exempt Support Personnel (SP) College or Department: COE: Pine Jog Environmental Education Center Location: Pine Jog Environmental Education Center Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 9:15 a.m. - 6:15 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-10-31 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position may close without prior notice. VETERANS’ PREFERENCE: Applicants may claim Veterans’ Preference on their application. The applicant claiming preference is responsible for providing required documentation at the time of making an application in Workday for a vacant position, or prior to the closing date of the vacancy announcement. If an applicant qualifies for Veterans' Preference and the SP position, they are shown preference by the guarantee of an interview. Veterans’ Preference does not guarantee a job. For additional information, please visit https://www.fau.edu/jobs/resources/veterans/. For assistance, please contact Recruitment Services at empl@fau.edu. APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume Cover Letter OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Anatomical-Sciences-Educator---Assistant-Associate-Full-Professor_REQ20298": {
      "title": "Anatomical Sciences Educator - Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: The Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine at Florida Atlantic University is seeking an innovative, dynamic and collaborative faculty member to serve as an Anatomical Sciences Educator in the undergraduate medical education (UME) curriculum.   The Anatomical Sciences Educator will join a team of faculty who teach throughout the pre-clerkship curriculum and will have a primary focus on integrated anatomy instruction in both classroom and laboratory settings.  In addition, the successful candidate will have opportunities to teach in other disciplines aligned with experience and expertise, such as pathology or histology.   The Anatomical Sciences Educator’s responsibilities are primarily: Teaching and Related Activities Create and present educational sessions that meet established learning objectives for anatomy instruction and collaborate with faculty to integrate material across courses. Serve as an anatomy lab instructor throughout the first-year curriculum, including all organ systems and structures covered in the Fundamentals of Biomedical Sciences course and the Neuroscience and Behavior course.  Assist in the creation of cadaveric prosected specimens for instructional use. Staff weekly open lab hours to provide additional guidance and support to students. Develop and conduct technology-based educational sessions.   Assist with preparation and administration of anatomy exams and assessments. Create and present educational sessions in other foundational sciences aligned with expertise such as embryology, histology, neuroscience, physiology and/or pathology. Serve as a facilitator for small group problem-based learning sessions (PBL, IQ, SLIQ) and other case-based teaching sessions. Serve as a course director within the UME program as opportunities arise. Participate in course grading committees and assist with course remediation as applicable. Assess and respond to quality improvement needs as applicable throughout the curriculum. Serve as an instructor in the College of Medicine graduate programs as opportunities arise. Advise and mentor medical students as well as graduate students and residents, as applicable. Scholarship and Related Activities Remain updated with advancements in anatomical sciences and medical education. Conduct scholarly work related to medical education, anatomy, pathology, histology, clinical practice, or other areas of interest. College of Medicine and University Service Serve on College of Medicine and University committees as required or requested. Clinical Activities Clinical work may be possible based on candidate qualifications and practice opportunities. Minimum Qualifications: • An MD or DO, or PhD in Anatomy or closely related field. • For MD and DO candidates, Florida medical licensure is required upon hire. ABMS or AOA board eligibility or certification is required. Desired Qualifications: • ABMS or AOA board specialization in Anatomic Pathology, Forensic Pathology, Surgery or other related discipline is preferred. • 3 to 5 years of teaching experience, preferably in classroom and laboratory settings • Experience in medical education • Experience in teaching anatomic dissection • Experienced use of technology-based instructional methods • Demonstrated track record of scholarship and closely related activities (i.e., invited lectures, enduring materials, peer-reviewed publications and/or grant-funded projects) Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: Charles E. Schmidt College of Medicine Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2027-01-27 Special Instructions to Applicant: This recruitment has been reopened; all previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: (1) a cover letter detailing their interest and how they qualify for this role, (2) a curriculum vitae, (3) copies of terminal or qualifying degrees and if applicable, documentation of board certification, and (4) any other relevant supporting documentation. Transcripts: The selected candidate for this position is required to submit an official transcript sent directly from the institution for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Similarly, for degrees from outside the United States, the evaluation by an organization belonging to the National Association of Credential Evaluation (NACES), with an indication of the documents the evaluation was prepared from (official transcripts, diplomas, dissertation abstracts) is required for the Provost’s credential file prior to the first day of employment. Transcripts must be issued to Florida Atlantic University, not to the individual applicant. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Internal-Auditor-Investigator_REQ23037": {
      "title": "Internal Auditor/Investigator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary:  Florida Atlantic University is seeking an Internal Auditor/Investigator - Boca Raton, FL.   Office of Inspector General (OIG) serves as an internal audit function with the purpose to strengthen the University and its Direct Support Organizations’ abilities to create, protect, and sustain value by providing the Board of Trustees (BOT), through its Audit and Compliance Committee (ACC), the University President, and Senior Management with independent, risk-based, and objective assurance, advice, insight, and foresight.       Summary of Responsibilities include:   Plans, performs, and produces reports for internal audits, investigations, management advisory, and operational reviews in accordance with professional standards and OIG internal policies and procedures. Conduct financial, operational, performance, Information technology, and compliance audit of various University departments, programs, and activities. Develop investigative plans and procedures to be performed for investigative assignments, under the supervision of the Inspector General or designee. Conduct interviews, collect supporting documentation, and review facts to substantiate conclusions in an audit or investigation. Performs at a high level and functions with long-term objectives in mind. Evaluates internal control systems and determines compliance with applicable statutes, rules, and regulations. Develop audit programs and procedures to be performed, including risk assessment, process analysis, and control evaluation. Test transactions (utilizing automated and/or traditional auditing methods) and analyze results of testing Prepare clear and concise working papers and other documentation supporting discussions, operational facts and results of testing to justify conclusions. Prepare complete and accurate audit and investigative reports, including those of a complex nature, and present written or oral reports to management, including discussing deficiencies and recommending corrective actions. Perform follow-up internal audits to evaluate management’s implementation of Action Plans Perform other related work and collaborate with other team members as assigned File documents, physically obtain information files from auditees, and perform inventories. FAU Benefits and Perks If Benefits & Perks are important to you, then FAU is the place to be! Working at FAU has its perks! In addition to helping drive change and having a positive impact by supporting our students, staff, and faculty, FAU offers: Excellent benefit packages including Medical (PPO/HMO $50 per month single & $180 per month family), Dental, Vision, Life Insurance, Flexible Spending plans, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and much more. State retirement options including tax-deferred annuities and Roth 403(b) plans. State employees Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. Sick Leave Pool Program. Paid time off (eligible employees) including vacation and sick leave, 1 personal day, 9 paid holidays, and paid winter break (at President’s discretion). Paid Community Engagement Volunteer Service Day Employee Educational Scholarship Program (EESP) for eligible Staff/Faculty - Tuition assistance after 6 months of full-time employment. For in-unit faculty, the EESP program may be extended to spouses and dependent children (eligibility rules apply). undefinedFor details on FAU's amazing offers visit us at https://www.fau.edu/hr/benefits/index.php   Explore Living in Palm Beach County The goal is to provide local employers and new employees in the area a comprehensive guide with places to live. View it here: Discover Housing Resources in Palm Beach County | BDB     Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience required. Special qualifications may be added to the minimum, such as possession of a Certified Public Accountant or a Certified Internal Auditor certificate. Other preferred certifications include, but are not limited to: Certified Information System Auditor (CISA) Certified Fraud Examiner (CFE) Certified Inspector General Auditor (CIGA) Certified Inspector General Investigator (CIGI) Certified Government Auditing Professional (CGAP) Certification in Risk Management Assurance (CRMA) Ability to effectively use Artificial Intelligence (AI) and other technological tools, including data analytics and audit platforms.\" Salary: $70,040 annually Exempt Administrative Managerial Professional (AMP) College or Department: Office of University Inspector General (OIG) Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: Monday - Friday, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Application Deadline: 2026-11-09 Special Instructions to Applicant: APPLICATION DOCUMENTS REQUIRED: Resume OFFICIAL SEALED TRANSCRIPTS REQUIRED: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. PRE-EMPLOYMENT SCREENINGS REQUIRED: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. REQUEST FOR ACCOMMODATIONS: Individuals with disabilities requiring accommodations may contact the Office of Civil Rights and Title IX at 561-297-3004 or send an email at accommodate@fau.edu. To contact Human Resources, please call 561-297-3057. For communication assistance call 7-1-1."
    },
    "https://fau.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/FAU/job/Boca-Raton/Executive-Director_REQ23066": {
      "title": "Executive Director",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nApply now to join FAU, where tomorrow begins. For more information on everything FAU has to offer, please visit www.fau.edu/jobs .  Note: Current FAU employees must apply as an internal applicant by logging into their existing Workday employee account. Position Summary: FAU Lab Schools seeks an entrepreneurial, data-informed, and results-oriented Executive Director to launch and lead The Carl A. DeSantis Center for Educational Strategy and Innovation (the Center). The Center is established through a $10 million, five-year catalytic investment from the Carl Angus DeSantis Foundation to scale the proven practices of FAU Lab Schools, a three-time National Blue Ribbon School of Excellence, across Palm Beach and Broward counties, throughout Florida, and nationally. The Executive Director serves as the chief architect and champion of the Center. The Executive Director will translate the Center’s five-year business plan into annual implementation plans, recruit and lead the Center team, manage the Foundation grant with full fiscal and programmatic accountability, and build the measurement systems, partnerships, and revenue streams that will sustain the Center beyond the initial investment. Position Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Center Expansion The Executive Director will establish the Center’s operating model and lead its expansion over the five-year grant period. Translate strategic initiatives into actionable implementation plans that identify responsibilities, milestones, deliverables, performance indicators, staffing, and costs. Develop a balanced portfolio that addresses immediate institutional and partner needs while advancing long-term innovation, measurable impact, scalability, and financial sustainability. Recruit and onboard Center staff and stand up core infrastructure, including the Learning Management System, continuing education registration, and event operations. Identify emerging challenges, research findings, technologies, and workforce needs in education, and translate them into programs, services, and partnerships. Create a disciplined process for evaluating, testing, launching, refining, and scaling new initiatives, and use evidence to decide which initiatives to expand, redesign, or discontinue. Professional Learning and Leadership Development The Executive Director will build a distinctive portfolio of learning experiences that connects research and practice for Florida educators and leaders. Assess emerging professional and organizational learning needs and developing scalable frameworks for educator development, leadership development, workforce preparation, and organizational improvement. Expand teacher and leader professional learning in coordination with the Stiles-Nicholson STEM Teacher Academy and leadership partners to meet or exceed performance targets. Develop and award micro-credentials and STEM certifications, and design LMS-based virtual courses that extend the Center’s reach. Design innovation-focused curricula that move leaders from compliance management to innovation architecture and prepare them to anticipate workforce needs. Apply principles of instructional design, adult learning, and talent development so that participants move beyond passive professional development to measurable changes in practice. Identify, recruit, and cultivate faculty, practitioners, industry experts, presenters, and nationally recognized subject-matter experts. School Model Scaling and Replication The Executive Director will position FAU Lab Schools as a national resource for schools and districts seeking proven, replicable models. Provide consulting and implementation support to partner districts. Expand the university lab school partner network across Florida and nationally. Support Center and research site visits annually for school and district leaders, educators, and policymakers. Develop and disseminate replication blueprints, toolkits, and implementation guides that document FAU Lab Schools programs and the conditions required for success. Engage school districts statewide, with the goal of reaching all 67 Florida school districts over the grant period. Partner with the FAU Lab Schools’ Research Director to expand Research Communities of Practice and the Action Research Fellows program to schools and districts statewide. Measurement, Evaluation, and Decision Science The Executive Director will ensure that significant decisions are informed by evidence and that initiatives are accompanied by quality performance measurements. Build and maintain a five-year outcome measurement framework for the Center objectives with definitions, baselines, annual targets, data sources, collection frequency, and responsible staff. Develop outcome performance measures to determine changes in teacher practice and leadership behavior. Use valid methods to demonstrate change, including matched pre- and post-assessments, follow-up after trainings and placements end, and verified methods for estimating student reach. Oversee the development of dashboards and decision-support tools that help leaders understand performance, anticipate challenges, and allocate resources. Partner with faculty, researchers, and data scientists to design studies, evaluate innovations, and advance responsible uses of artificial intelligence and predictive analytics in education. Establish continuous feedback loops that use outcome data, stakeholder input, and financial results to improve programs and guide future investment. Grant Management, Compliance, and Donor Stewardship The Executive Director will serve as the primary steward of the Center’s relationship with the Carl Angus DeSantis Foundation. Manage the Foundation grant in accordance with the grant agreement, approved annual budgets, and performance commitments. Prepare mid-year and year-end programmatic and financial reports that compare actual performance and expenditures to annual targets, explain material variances, and describe lessons learned and corrective actions. Oversee accurate tracking and reporting of participants, activities, results, and expenditures by county. Maintain clear separation between the catalytic grant and other awards. Partnerships, Dissemination, and Thought Leadership The Executive Director will serve as a highly visible ambassador for the Center and ensure that what the Center learns is shared. Establish strategic partnerships with universities, school districts, government agencies, foundations, corporations, organizations, and research institutions. Develop external advisory relationships and networks that allow the Center to continuously identify emerging trends, opportunities, technologies, research, and promising practices. Position the Center as a trusted convener where leaders from education, research, business, government, and philanthropy collaborate on significant challenges. Develop a dissemination strategy that includes publications, policy briefs, practitioner guides, case studies, digital resources, and presentations at state and national conferences. Translate complex research and analytical results into clear, actionable information for practitioners, policymakers, and donors. Represent the Center with senior university, education, government, philanthropic, corporate, and community leaders. Financial Sustainability and Growth The Executive Director will treat the $10 million investment as the catalyst, not the ceiling, and build a diversified model for long-term sustainability. Collaborate with the FAU Lab Schools’ leadership on developing additional revenue streams to support the Center. Develop business cases for major initiatives that weigh demand, strategic alignment, anticipated impact, required investment, scalability, and sustainability. Support the cultivation of relationships with foundations, donors, corporations, and government entities capable of supporting or scaling the Center’s work. Manage budgets, personnel, contracts, vendors, and timelines with a high degree of accountability and fiscal responsibility. Team and Organizational Leadership The Executive Director will build a culture defined by curiosity, analytical rigor, execution, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Recruit, develop, and lead a high-performing multidisciplinary team capable of working across education, research, analytics, professional learning, business development, communications, and program implementation. Coordinate with FAU Lab Schools’ staff and faculty, as needed. Establish clear priorities, responsibilities, performance expectations, and accountability. Lead cross-functional initiatives that involve multiple university units, FAU colleges, and external organizations. Communicate strategy, evidence, performance, and recommendations to the Superintendent, university and school leadership, and the Foundation. Create an environment in which responsible experimentation is encouraged, results are measured, lessons are captured, and successful innovations are rapidly translated into broader practice. Minimum Qualifications: • Master’s degree or higher in education, business, instructional design, organizational leadership, or a related field. • Five or more years of experience as a school district senior leader or principal supervisor, OR ten or more years of experience as a school principal and school district leader. • Five or more years of experience building programs or strategic initiatives from concept through implementation, evaluation, and scale. • Experience managing grants or restricted funds, including budgets, compliance, and programmatic and financial reporting. • Demonstrated ability to use data, research, and performance measures to inform strategy and decision making. • Experience managing complex budgets, personnel, contracts, timelines, and external partners. • Exceptional executive communication, presentation, relationship-building, analytical, and leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications and Experience • Doctorate in education, organizational leadership, or a related field. • Knowledge of Florida K–12 education, school district operations, and educator preparation and leadership systems. • Knowledge of program evaluation, research design, key performance indicators, dashboards, and decision-science approaches. • Understanding of instructional design, learning science, adult learning, and learning management systems. • Experience developing conferences, institutes, speaker series, or other large-scale professional convenings. • Experience with university–K–12 partnerships, laboratory schools, or STEM, health care, or research workforce pathways. • Demonstrated success in donor stewardship and in building partnerships across education, government, business, philanthropy, and health care. • Experience generating sustainable revenue through grants, philanthropy, sponsorships, consulting, licensing, or fee-based programming. • Demonstrated ability to lead multidisciplinary teams and align diverse stakeholders around common objectives. Salary: Commensurate with Experience College or Department: FAU Lab Schools Location: Boca Raton Work Days and Hours: N/A Application Deadline: 2026-11-09 Special Instructions to Applicant: This position is open until filled and may close without prior notice. This position is subject to funding. All applicants must apply electronically to the currently posted position on the Office of Human Resources' job website (https://fau.edu/jobs) by completing the required employment application for this recruitment and submitting the related documents. Required Documents: FAU’s Career Page permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. PLEASE NOTE: A maximum of five (5) documents may be attached to your application. If more than five (5) documents are required for submission, please combine additional documents into a single attachment to not exceed the maximum permitted. The site permits the attachment of required/requested documentation. Candidates wishing full consideration are to provide the following: a cover letter and resume. Transcripts: Final candidate will be required to have official, sealed transcripts and original NACES evaluation, if applicable, sent from their educational institution to Human Resources prior to the start of employment. Background Screening: Selected candidates must successfully complete and pass all employment screenings prior to the start of employment. Employment screenings may include a criminal background check (level I and level II), motor vehicle check, credit check, reference checks, alcohol, and drug screening check. The candidate selected for the position will be required to have fingerprinting done at the FAU Police Department and a background check done by the school. Accommodations: Individuals requiring accommodation, please call 561-297-3057. 711"
    }
  },
